1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:02:03,810
Visit our website for more: turkision.com

2
00:02:04,035 --> 00:02:07,675
No living being was harmed
during the filming of this series.

3
00:02:36,520 --> 00:02:38,879
Allah is the Greatest!

4
00:03:19,560 --> 00:03:22,919
Stay away from the windows!
There are archers everywhere!

5
00:03:23,200 --> 00:03:25,559
They surrounded this side too, Malhun Hatun.

6
00:03:25,800 --> 00:03:27,799
Everything is on fire!

7
00:03:28,280 --> 00:03:29,999
What are we going to do?

8
00:03:33,960 --> 00:03:38,279
Brother, we won't be able to get out
of the windows, they are everywhere!

9
00:03:42,480 --> 00:03:44,839
Then we will get out of the door!

10
00:04:07,200 --> 00:04:09,319
In the name of Allah!

11
00:04:16,320 --> 00:04:18,399
In the name of Allah!

12
00:04:20,399 --> 00:04:22,599
Come on, Alaaddin.

13
00:04:32,320 --> 00:04:34,999
Come on, Alaeddin, let's find
our mother!

14
00:04:35,680 --> 00:04:37,199
We will get out, my daughter.

15
00:04:38,480 --> 00:04:40,919
We will get out.

16
00:04:48,720 --> 00:04:50,719
In the name of Allah!

17
00:04:51,440 --> 00:04:52,479
Alaaddin.

18
00:04:52,480 --> 00:04:53,959
In the name of Allah!

19
00:04:55,120 --> 00:04:56,799
My son.

20
00:04:56,800 --> 00:04:59,399
Come, my girl.

21
00:04:59,560 --> 00:05:01,759
Come on, son!

22
00:05:04,840 --> 00:05:06,359
Son!

23
00:05:09,680 --> 00:05:10,799
Come on.

24
00:05:10,840 --> 00:05:12,279
Alaaddin, open the door!

25
00:05:18,160 --> 00:05:19,999
Alaaddin, with shields!

26
00:05:22,600 --> 00:05:25,559
In the name of Allah!

27
00:05:26,120 --> 00:05:28,679
Mother!

28
00:05:30,840 --> 00:05:31,919
Are you okay?

29
00:05:31,920 --> 00:05:32,519
We are fine.

30
00:05:32,520 --> 00:05:33,599
How is my sister?

31
00:05:33,600 --> 00:05:37,319
We are fine, the Hatuns
are at the diwan, they need help.

32
00:05:45,200 --> 00:05:47,439
Come on, sons, go!

33
00:05:58,160 --> 00:06:02,559
I will make you regret coming to my
house and trying to harm my children!

34
00:06:03,400 --> 00:06:05,919
Alps! Put out the fire!

35
00:06:10,240 --> 00:06:11,679
Come on, Hüseyin.

36
00:06:12,320 --> 00:06:16,999
We will see who is stronger now!

37
00:06:17,520 --> 00:06:18,799
Come on.

38
00:07:37,520 --> 00:07:40,959
Come on, Alps, we are
going to support Osman Bey.

39
00:07:46,400 --> 00:07:47,679
Alaaddin!

40
00:08:14,280 --> 00:08:16,679
Hatuns! Are you there?

41
00:08:20,880 --> 00:08:22,359
Bayindir?

42
00:08:22,760 --> 00:08:24,079
Bayindir, come on.

43
00:08:24,080 --> 00:08:26,799
Step back, I will break the door.

44
00:08:42,029 --> 00:08:44,789
The infidels are everywhere, they
want to burn down the palace.

45
00:08:44,800 --> 00:08:46,879
But we will get out of
here, Inshallah, come on.

46
00:08:46,880 --> 00:08:48,399
Come on.

47
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:53,159
Damned infidels!

48
00:09:05,200 --> 00:09:06,599
Come on, hatuns!

49
00:09:06,600 --> 00:09:07,439
Come on.

50
00:10:12,920 --> 00:10:14,679
This is the battlefield, Osman Bey.

51
00:10:14,680 --> 00:10:17,919
But, you need to go to Yenişehir.
There isn't anyone to protect them there.

52
00:10:17,920 --> 00:10:19,919
I won’t leave you alone here.

53
00:10:25,560 --> 00:10:27,439
Don't worry about here.
I have it under control.

54
00:10:27,440 --> 00:10:28,039
Turgut.

55
00:10:28,040 --> 00:10:32,839
Osman Bey, if Yenişehir falls, this
battle we have here won't mean anything.

56
00:10:35,760 --> 00:10:37,039
Come on, Osman Bey.

57
00:10:37,040 --> 00:10:37,679
Come on.

58
00:10:37,680 --> 00:10:38,799
You're right.

59
00:10:38,800 --> 00:10:40,999
If the palace fall,
our honor will fall with it.

60
00:10:41,480 --> 00:10:42,799
Alps.

61
00:10:42,800 --> 00:10:44,879
We're going to Yenişehir.
Come on.

62
00:10:45,120 --> 00:10:46,279
Thank you.

63
00:11:06,120 --> 00:11:11,519
Come on, we won't stop
until we reach Yenişehir. Come on.

64
00:11:17,840 --> 00:11:19,039
Come on.

65
00:11:23,840 --> 00:11:26,599
Don't let them run away from here!

66
00:11:31,600 --> 00:11:32,799
Bala.

67
00:11:42,400 --> 00:11:44,079
Did they go?

68
00:11:44,640 --> 00:11:46,839
Kill them!

69
00:11:47,680 --> 00:11:50,759
No one will leave this place alive.

70
00:12:31,120 --> 00:12:32,879
Bala.

71
00:12:32,880 --> 00:12:35,479
Halime.

72
00:13:17,520 --> 00:13:18,399
Halime.

73
00:13:19,560 --> 00:13:20,639
Halime.

74
00:13:26,360 --> 00:13:27,799
Mother, are you okay?

75
00:13:34,240 --> 00:13:35,759
Mother.

76
00:13:36,760 --> 00:13:38,919
Mother.

77
00:13:39,200 --> 00:13:40,199
Aunt!

78
00:13:40,200 --> 00:13:41,799
Bala.

79
00:13:41,800 --> 00:13:43,799
Protect Bala.

80
00:13:45,280 --> 00:13:46,919
Aunt!

81
00:13:50,120 --> 00:13:51,519
Are you okay, mother?

82
00:13:51,720 --> 00:13:53,599
Bala.

83
00:13:53,600 --> 00:13:55,079
Esma.

84
00:15:00,120 --> 00:15:02,399
Alaaddin.
Orhan.

85
00:15:06,320 --> 00:15:07,879
Are you okay?

86
00:15:07,880 --> 00:15:09,399
- We're okay.
- We're okay.

87
00:15:10,080 --> 00:15:12,319
You walk towards the fire, huh?

88
00:15:12,320 --> 00:15:15,239
Come here.

89
00:15:16,680 --> 00:15:18,479
Come here.

90
00:15:18,480 --> 00:15:19,719
Come.

91
00:15:19,720 --> 00:15:21,959
You will burn!

92
00:15:21,960 --> 00:15:23,599
You will burn alive.

93
00:15:23,600 --> 00:15:25,599
Look at me.

94
00:15:27,720 --> 00:15:29,239
Get up.

95
00:15:30,560 --> 00:15:32,879
Get up.
Get. Up.

96
00:15:34,040 --> 00:15:35,839
Kneel.

97
00:15:41,680 --> 00:15:45,079
You attacked my home...

98
00:15:45,080 --> 00:15:48,039
my Hatuns and kids, huh?

99
00:15:48,040 --> 00:15:51,599
Did you think you were going to
make it out alive?

100
00:16:01,840 --> 00:16:03,479
This is your end.

101
00:16:09,200 --> 00:16:10,959
Malhun.

102
00:16:11,760 --> 00:16:12,959
Malhun..

103
00:16:13,160 --> 00:16:14,359
Osman.

104
00:16:14,920 --> 00:16:15,999
Are you okay?

105
00:16:16,160 --> 00:16:17,839
I am okay.

106
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:19,119
My sons...

107
00:16:19,320 --> 00:16:20,599
Orhan, Alaaddin..

108
00:16:20,800 --> 00:16:21,319
We're fine.

109
00:16:21,520 --> 00:16:22,839
Osman...

110
00:16:23,240 --> 00:16:25,479
Halime and Bala...

111
00:16:26,960 --> 00:16:28,799
Go!

112
00:16:29,600 --> 00:16:30,599
Move!

113
00:16:37,800 --> 00:16:39,399
Traitor...

114
00:16:41,400 --> 00:16:42,439
Osman!

115
00:16:42,600 --> 00:16:44,479
Bayındır helped us.

116
00:16:50,320 --> 00:16:53,479
I will deal with you later.

117
00:16:57,760 --> 00:17:00,359
Alps, put the fire out!

118
00:17:00,440 --> 00:17:01,079
Come on.

119
00:17:01,280 --> 00:17:03,429
My sons.

120
00:17:03,449 --> 00:17:03,928
Let's go.

121
00:17:04,400 --> 00:17:05,719
- Let's go!
- Hurry up!

122
00:17:05,920 --> 00:17:09,279
Move!

123
00:17:11,240 --> 00:17:14,159
Ya Shafi!

124
00:17:14,440 --> 00:17:16,877
Give me my bag, Ülgen!

125
00:17:17,040 --> 00:17:18,559
We have to make an ointment.

126
00:17:18,640 --> 00:17:20,396
Bring it!

127
00:17:21,040 --> 00:17:21,959
Ülgen!

128
00:17:22,200 --> 00:17:24,637
We will cauterize the wound.
Tell the Alps...

129
00:17:24,660 --> 00:17:26,498
...to bring embers.

130
00:17:36,920 --> 00:17:38,479
Dark midwife.

131
00:17:38,680 --> 00:17:40,239
Her arm is wounded too.

132
00:17:40,360 --> 00:17:42,999
Put pressure on it.

133
00:17:46,280 --> 00:17:47,999
Dogs...

134
00:17:48,440 --> 00:17:50,599
Not even an
enemy would do this.

135
00:17:51,240 --> 00:17:55,639
They tried to burn us here alive
because they are afraid to face us.

136
00:18:00,080 --> 00:18:01,959
Bala...

137
00:18:06,800 --> 00:18:08,599
Bala!

138
00:18:12,120 --> 00:18:13,999
Bala.

139
00:18:14,800 --> 00:18:16,399
Bala!

140
00:18:17,160 --> 00:18:18,399
Bala!

141
00:18:27,240 --> 00:18:28,999
Bala!

142
00:18:29,880 --> 00:18:31,079
Are you okay, Bala?

143
00:18:31,600 --> 00:18:32,199
Bala...

144
00:18:32,360 --> 00:18:33,159
Dark midwife, tell me...

145
00:18:33,600 --> 00:18:34,399
She's okay.

146
00:18:34,800 --> 00:18:36,199
She will be fine, my Bey.

147
00:18:37,840 --> 00:18:38,999
She's a mother...

148
00:18:39,200 --> 00:18:40,919
and mothers are strong.

149
00:18:41,160 --> 00:18:44,079
They protect their children
with their lives.

150
00:18:44,400 --> 00:18:45,359
They're strong!

151
00:18:45,640 --> 00:18:47,159
Don't you worry.

152
00:18:53,440 --> 00:18:56,039
Are you hurt, my Bey?

153
00:18:56,800 --> 00:18:59,719
I'm fine.

154
00:18:59,920 --> 00:19:01,319
Bala..

155
00:19:08,400 --> 00:19:09,639
Halime...

156
00:19:18,640 --> 00:19:20,559
Halime!

157
00:19:22,800 --> 00:19:24,599
Bala!

158
00:19:27,880 --> 00:19:29,279
Halime!

159
00:19:31,360 --> 00:19:32,639
What is this?

160
00:19:33,000 --> 00:19:34,519
What is this?

161
00:19:34,800 --> 00:19:36,599
Halime is fine, Osman Bey.

162
00:19:36,960 --> 00:19:38,559
Alçiçek is making her sleep.

163
00:19:38,720 --> 00:19:40,759
She's alright.

164
00:19:46,840 --> 00:19:48,799
Tell me what happened.

165
00:19:48,920 --> 00:19:51,879
I want to know everything.

166
00:20:02,400 --> 00:20:04,559
My child...

167
00:20:05,080 --> 00:20:06,519
You're going to be fine.

168
00:20:42,000 --> 00:20:44,079
Osman ran away...

169
00:20:44,480 --> 00:20:48,999
but I have you, Turgut.

170
00:20:49,200 --> 00:20:51,359
I will separate your skin...

171
00:20:51,600 --> 00:20:53,479
from your bones.

172
00:20:53,840 --> 00:20:57,959
You're mistaken, Nayman.
My people don't run away.

173
00:20:58,160 --> 00:20:59,839
He’ll show up...

174
00:21:00,200 --> 00:21:03,199
in such an unexpected time that...

175
00:21:04,720 --> 00:21:06,399
you won't see him coming here.

176
00:21:06,600 --> 00:21:08,599
I will kill everyone...

177
00:21:09,400 --> 00:21:12,639
who are against me.

178
00:21:14,320 --> 00:21:17,079
It’s your turn now, Turgut.

179
00:21:18,680 --> 00:21:20,999
We live for martyrdom.

180
00:21:21,600 --> 00:21:23,799
I can die gladly.

181
00:21:23,960 --> 00:21:26,519
However, the ones after us...

182
00:21:27,200 --> 00:21:31,479
will spread the words of Allah, Inshallah.

183
00:21:32,200 --> 00:21:34,919
Do whatever you're going to do!

184
00:21:35,200 --> 00:21:36,519
What are you waiting for?

185
00:21:36,520 --> 00:21:38,039
What are you waiting for?

186
00:21:38,240 --> 00:21:39,319
Come on!

187
00:21:56,440 --> 00:21:57,639
Look...

188
00:21:57,800 --> 00:21:58,999
Take a good look...

189
00:21:59,600 --> 00:22:01,399
Brother...

190
00:22:02,640 --> 00:22:04,399
My Bey.

191
00:22:08,200 --> 00:22:09,639
Kutan.

192
00:22:09,840 --> 00:22:14,479
It was an honor for me to walk this
road with you, Turgut Bey.

193
00:22:18,160 --> 00:22:20,319
Will you give me your blessing?

194
00:22:20,560 --> 00:22:21,959
Kutan.

195
00:22:22,040 --> 00:22:23,919
Will you, my Bey?

196
00:22:27,000 --> 00:22:28,079
My Bey?

197
00:22:28,440 --> 00:22:31,519
Of course, brother, I give
you my blessing.

198
00:22:37,240 --> 00:22:41,719
I bear witness that there
is no deity but Allah...

199
00:22:42,040 --> 00:22:44,479
Don't do it, kill me instead of him!

200
00:22:46,800 --> 00:22:47,959
Kutan.

201
00:22:48,600 --> 00:22:50,239
Kutan.

202
00:22:54,600 --> 00:22:56,439
Nayman.

203
00:23:00,240 --> 00:23:01,239
Acar...

204
00:23:01,440 --> 00:23:05,279
The soldiers of Islam die once
but we will be reborn as thousands!

205
00:23:05,400 --> 00:23:08,199
You will lose your head, too, Nayman!

206
00:23:08,720 --> 00:23:11,879
My Bey, will you give me your blessing?

207
00:23:14,960 --> 00:23:17,399
I give you my blessing, brother.

208
00:23:17,640 --> 00:23:20,319
I bear witness that there
is no deity but Allah...

209
00:23:20,319 --> 00:23:24,889
and I bear witness that Muhammed is
His servant and messenger.

210
00:23:39,400 --> 00:23:41,199
Nayman!

211
00:23:42,640 --> 00:23:45,959
Even if you go to hell..

212
00:23:46,160 --> 00:23:49,279
I will come and find you!

213
00:24:11,640 --> 00:24:13,199
Malhun!

214
00:24:14,320 --> 00:24:16,999
Prepare all of the Alps.

215
00:24:18,920 --> 00:24:21,599
Yenişehir will become a
powerful place.

216
00:24:21,800 --> 00:24:26,079
Put archers on top
of the walls and towers.

217
00:24:26,800 --> 00:24:29,599
No one will move
without my knowledge.

218
00:24:31,180 --> 00:24:31,779
Boran.

219
00:24:31,800 --> 00:24:32,599
My Bey.

220
00:24:32,760 --> 00:24:36,639
Prepare the soldiers.
We will go help Turgut Bey.

221
00:24:37,160 --> 00:24:38,719
Your command, my Bey.

222
00:24:40,520 --> 00:24:41,319
Cerkutay.

223
00:24:41,400 --> 00:24:42,079
My Bey.

224
00:24:42,080 --> 00:24:46,919
You will learn how many horsemen
and infantry they have.

225
00:24:47,200 --> 00:24:49,039
Your command, my Bey.

226
00:24:49,600 --> 00:24:50,279
Baysungur.

227
00:24:50,280 --> 00:24:51,349
My Bey.

228
00:24:51,680 --> 00:24:55,479
You will call everyone in the surrounding
tribes to Söğüt and Yenişehir.

229
00:24:56,080 --> 00:24:57,999
Your command, my Bey.

230
00:24:59,400 --> 00:24:59,959
Gürbüz.

231
00:25:00,080 --> 00:25:00,999
My Bey.

232
00:25:01,200 --> 00:25:03,439
You will go to Nayman's headquarters.

233
00:25:03,440 --> 00:25:07,599
You will learn who goes there.

234
00:25:07,720 --> 00:25:08,959
Your command, my Bey.

235
00:25:09,520 --> 00:25:10,599
Your command, my Bey.

236
00:25:23,840 --> 00:25:25,399
Osman.

237
00:25:25,800 --> 00:25:28,399
What about Bayindir?
What are we going to do with him?

238
00:25:29,840 --> 00:25:33,839
If he wasn't here, things would be worse.

239
00:25:34,440 --> 00:25:37,399
I will deal with him.

240
00:25:40,360 --> 00:25:41,599
Malhun.

241
00:25:42,600 --> 00:25:44,919
The children and Yenişehir
are in your care.

242
00:25:45,240 --> 00:25:47,719
I will go to the headquarters
with Boran.

243
00:25:48,080 --> 00:25:49,599
Don't worry.

244
00:26:35,920 --> 00:26:37,319
Turgut Bey...

245
00:26:39,720 --> 00:26:41,519
Turgut Bey...

246
00:26:46,560 --> 00:26:48,279
Osman Bey!

247
00:26:55,320 --> 00:26:57,399
How did they escape?

248
00:27:01,200 --> 00:27:03,919
What were you doing, Celali?

249
00:27:04,160 --> 00:27:08,359
Mother Sultan, as soon as Osman
learned about Yenişehir...

250
00:27:08,520 --> 00:27:09,719
he returned to the palace.

251
00:27:10,000 --> 00:27:13,999
Otherwise, it was impossible for Hatuns to survive.

252
00:27:25,320 --> 00:27:26,959
Bayındır.

253
00:27:27,720 --> 00:27:29,999
Where is he?

254
00:27:31,000 --> 00:27:33,239
If Osman captures him...

255
00:27:33,880 --> 00:27:35,919
he will learn everything.

256
00:27:36,880 --> 00:27:39,679
That I worked with Nayman.

257
00:27:43,520 --> 00:27:45,199
There is no news...

258
00:27:46,400 --> 00:27:49,199
from Bayindir and Hüseyin, Mother Sultan.

259
00:27:53,400 --> 00:27:56,799
They couldn't do the job!
Fools!

260
00:28:02,480 --> 00:28:03,679
No!

261
00:28:04,840 --> 00:28:07,639
It's not okay to stay here now.

262
00:28:10,920 --> 00:28:13,999
Prepare the horses, we are leaving.

263
00:28:26,120 --> 00:28:27,199
My Bey.

264
00:28:40,800 --> 00:28:43,199
I have Turgut.

265
00:28:50,360 --> 00:28:53,159
I give you 15 days.

266
00:28:53,560 --> 00:28:56,309
Your Alps and people will
drop their weapons.

267
00:28:56,640 --> 00:29:01,199
If you make any move, I will
kill Turgut and, then your people.

268
00:29:07,400 --> 00:29:10,679
If you go under my rule, you can live.

269
00:29:27,480 --> 00:29:30,719
I will never give my people to you...

270
00:29:31,040 --> 00:29:33,559
or give Turgut to you.

271
00:29:35,960 --> 00:29:40,759
You have a seal and you have so many
cruel men behind you.

272
00:29:41,400 --> 00:29:43,919
I swear...

273
00:29:44,800 --> 00:29:48,319
I'm going to make
these lands your grave.

274
00:29:48,320 --> 00:29:51,119
I swear!

275
00:29:54,280 --> 00:29:57,479
2 weeks later

276
00:30:24,480 --> 00:30:27,119
It's time, huh, Osman?

277
00:30:27,800 --> 00:30:29,759
You're right, Bala.

278
00:30:30,520 --> 00:30:32,679
It’s time.

279
00:30:33,000 --> 00:30:34,999
We've been waiting for
this day for a long time.

280
00:30:35,000 --> 00:30:37,119
May it be Mubarak. (holy)

281
00:30:40,320 --> 00:30:42,399
But..

282
00:30:44,480 --> 00:30:47,479
Tell me.

283
00:30:48,680 --> 00:30:52,959
Is it the right time?

284
00:30:56,320 --> 00:30:59,279
A tree that doesn't root
during hard times...

285
00:30:59,280 --> 00:31:02,079
would crumble with a breeze of wind.

286
00:31:03,200 --> 00:31:05,559
We'll try now, Bala.

287
00:31:06,760 --> 00:31:09,479
May Allah help you.

288
00:31:09,480 --> 00:31:10,799
Amin.

289
00:31:11,960 --> 00:31:14,399
Amin, Inshallah.

290
00:31:17,400 --> 00:31:18,999
Come on.

291
00:31:30,960 --> 00:31:33,399
These need one more emery.

292
00:31:34,400 --> 00:31:35,999
Mother.

293
00:31:36,000 --> 00:31:37,599
Come and take a look.

294
00:31:47,160 --> 00:31:49,279
Do it one more time.

295
00:31:49,280 --> 00:31:51,519
Carefully.

296
00:31:51,520 --> 00:31:53,919
We'll prepare it
right away, Malhun Hatun.

297
00:32:01,120 --> 00:32:03,079
You're tired.

298
00:32:03,600 --> 00:32:07,999
You don't ever sleep but it will be
worth your efforts, Inshallah.

299
00:32:08,000 --> 00:32:09,679
Inshallah.

300
00:32:11,200 --> 00:32:12,999
Mashallah.

301
00:32:13,000 --> 00:32:16,599
Mashallah.

302
00:32:17,280 --> 00:32:19,719
Beat it, valiants, beat it.

303
00:32:19,720 --> 00:32:21,599
Beat it.

304
00:32:21,920 --> 00:32:24,599
Beat it like you're beating infidels!

305
00:32:24,600 --> 00:32:27,399
Beat it for your late master.

306
00:32:29,880 --> 00:32:32,239
A martyr's blood...

307
00:32:32,560 --> 00:32:35,039
and a craftsman's sweat.

308
00:32:35,040 --> 00:32:38,679
If those two are there, a piece of
land becomes a nation.

309
00:32:39,560 --> 00:32:41,599
We went through a lot.

310
00:32:41,600 --> 00:32:43,479
We will go through more but...

311
00:32:43,480 --> 00:32:46,319
we won't stop!

312
00:32:48,800 --> 00:32:51,879
It was waiting for the right
time and now it is.

313
00:32:52,760 --> 00:32:53,999
It is.

314
00:32:54,000 --> 00:32:55,719
It is, brother.

315
00:33:04,840 --> 00:33:07,119
Okay. This is good.

316
00:33:07,120 --> 00:33:08,879
Thank you for your work.

317
00:33:09,400 --> 00:33:13,159
Come on, move the tables to the square.

318
00:33:13,160 --> 00:33:15,879
Good work.

319
00:33:16,480 --> 00:33:17,959
Good work.

320
00:33:22,200 --> 00:33:23,399
Hadrat Sultan...

321
00:33:23,640 --> 00:33:26,959
there's a letter from Osman Bey.

322
00:33:27,680 --> 00:33:28,999
Hand it over, Vizier.

323
00:33:34,200 --> 00:33:37,839
Let's see what Osman Bey
wants from us.

324
00:33:45,520 --> 00:33:47,679
Hadrat Sultan...

325
00:33:48,400 --> 00:33:55,159
I’m going into battle for defeating the
Mongols who once were in your palace.

326
00:33:55,160 --> 00:33:58,159
That's why I...

327
00:33:58,160 --> 00:34:01,559
would wish to see the
soldiers you once promised.

328
00:34:09,800 --> 00:34:11,319
Osman Bey...

329
00:34:12,360 --> 00:34:14,998
is asking for the soldiers
I've promised to him.

330
00:34:15,600 --> 00:34:16,998
My Sultan.

331
00:34:17,400 --> 00:34:19,319
Excuse me...

332
00:34:19,320 --> 00:34:21,359
but my opinion is...

333
00:34:21,360 --> 00:34:23,039
that Nayman has the seal...

334
00:34:23,600 --> 00:34:27,039
and that makes me doubt if we should
be his enemy.

335
00:34:27,600 --> 00:34:29,319
Since when..

336
00:34:29,960 --> 00:34:32,799
do you question the Sultan's orders?

337
00:34:35,920 --> 00:34:37,199
Clerk.

338
00:34:37,199 --> 00:34:38,737
Write this.

339
00:34:44,400 --> 00:34:49,119
May Osman Bey's sword be sharp
and his fight be victorious.

340
00:34:49,120 --> 00:34:51,399
The army he wishes for...

341
00:34:51,760 --> 00:34:53,958
will be given to him.

342
00:35:05,560 --> 00:35:07,119
Vizier.

343
00:35:07,840 --> 00:35:09,759
You can leave.

344
00:35:11,040 --> 00:35:13,359
I'm going to talk to Sultan...

345
00:35:14,000 --> 00:35:16,039
alone.

346
00:35:27,840 --> 00:35:29,399
Everyone leave.

347
00:35:41,120 --> 00:35:45,279
When a lot of traitors
have roamed this palace...

348
00:35:45,560 --> 00:35:50,559
do you think I would give you a
Vizier who is not loyal to me?

349
00:35:56,400 --> 00:36:00,959
You won't make any moves
against Nayman.

350
00:36:01,400 --> 00:36:02,799
Because..

351
00:36:02,800 --> 00:36:05,479
I've given the seal to him.

352
00:36:24,120 --> 00:36:27,639
Let's see...

353
00:36:36,080 --> 00:36:39,559
In the name of Allah, the most
gracious and the most merciful.

354
00:36:53,560 --> 00:36:57,119
Well...

355
00:37:01,360 --> 00:37:03,839
Now...

356
00:37:25,520 --> 00:37:27,799
My Sheikh.

357
00:37:49,480 --> 00:37:52,759
In the name of Allah, the most
gracious and the most merciful

358
00:37:53,600 --> 00:37:56,119
Oh, Allah!

359
00:38:09,720 --> 00:38:11,599
My Sheikh.

360
00:38:16,200 --> 00:38:18,479
Let me see...

361
00:38:20,960 --> 00:38:23,799
Mashallah...

362
00:38:35,760 --> 00:38:38,119
The sizes are pretty similar.

363
00:38:39,200 --> 00:38:40,479
InshaIIah...

364
00:38:40,960 --> 00:38:43,759
when these are done...

365
00:38:44,160 --> 00:38:45,799
then...

366
00:38:46,000 --> 00:38:50,159
we will pay all merchants
with this silver coin.

367
00:38:50,360 --> 00:38:54,519
We will use these to pay
for all caravans.

368
00:39:01,200 --> 00:39:03,399
Blacksmiths...

369
00:39:04,120 --> 00:39:06,359
you have a crucial task
ahead of you.

370
00:39:06,920 --> 00:39:10,999
Start making these at once.

371
00:39:11,240 --> 00:39:12,639
Your command, my Bey.

372
00:39:12,800 --> 00:39:14,679
But..

373
00:39:15,040 --> 00:39:16,679
look at the sides.

374
00:39:16,840 --> 00:39:18,559
I want you to...

375
00:39:19,000 --> 00:39:20,559
fix them as well.

376
00:39:20,720 --> 00:39:23,799
Your command, my Bey.

377
00:39:30,600 --> 00:39:32,399
40 of these..

378
00:39:32,880 --> 00:39:36,799
will let you gather a caravan.

379
00:39:37,400 --> 00:39:41,599
40 of them will pay for 50 swords.

380
00:39:44,400 --> 00:39:48,039
Nayman gave us 15 days to surrender.

381
00:39:48,920 --> 00:39:52,279
So before that time runs out..

382
00:39:52,840 --> 00:39:55,759
we will do what needs to
be done for our freedom.

383
00:39:56,360 --> 00:40:00,679
Inshallah.

384
00:40:00,840 --> 00:40:05,119
May Allah keep you
in His path, Osman Bey.

385
00:40:06,400 --> 00:40:08,399
You're planning to
do a good deed.

386
00:40:09,000 --> 00:40:10,559
May it end well for all of you.

387
00:40:10,840 --> 00:40:12,279
Inshallah, my Sheikh.

388
00:40:12,640 --> 00:40:13,559
InshalIah.

389
00:40:14,160 --> 00:40:16,039
Once the coins are all done..

390
00:40:16,600 --> 00:40:20,199
we will use them
to pay for all our trades.

391
00:40:23,360 --> 00:40:26,359
That way, it will spread even faster.

392
00:40:27,160 --> 00:40:31,639
Inshallah, our coins will be used
to trade all over these lands.

393
00:40:32,200 --> 00:40:33,199
Inshallah.

394
00:40:33,360 --> 00:40:35,679
Inshallah, my Sheihh.

395
00:40:39,560 --> 00:40:41,199
Inshallah, my Sheikh.

396
00:40:41,960 --> 00:40:44,119
Kumral Abdal.

397
00:40:45,520 --> 00:40:47,559
Gather iron, silver and copper...

398
00:40:48,120 --> 00:40:49,959
Sort them all out..

399
00:40:50,130 --> 00:40:52,249
and prepare them to be forged.

400
00:40:52,640 --> 00:40:54,519
Get it done by tomorrow.

401
00:40:57,040 --> 00:40:59,999
Inshallah, we will see this
done Osman Bey...

402
00:41:01,000 --> 00:41:03,959
but how are we going to hit Nayman?

403
00:41:07,600 --> 00:41:11,319
Sultan Alaaddin promised to
send us an army.

404
00:41:14,720 --> 00:41:19,879
The army will encourage
the Beys to stand by our side.

405
00:41:22,080 --> 00:41:24,159
Let’s wait until the army is here.

406
00:41:26,040 --> 00:41:29,159
If your intention is to hit
Nayman, Osman Bey...

407
00:41:29,720 --> 00:41:32,959
all Alps of our tribe will follow you.

408
00:41:35,000 --> 00:41:36,879
Isn't that right, Aktemur Bey?

409
00:41:37,560 --> 00:41:38,319
Yes!

410
00:41:40,600 --> 00:41:42,999
Your command, my Bey.

411
00:41:43,280 --> 00:41:46,019
Thank you...

412
00:41:47,120 --> 00:41:50,119
but there's a time for everything.

413
00:41:51,520 --> 00:41:54,119
We have something
else to deal with for now.

414
00:41:55,120 --> 00:41:56,239
My Sheikh...

415
00:41:56,600 --> 00:41:58,919
let's make our sacrifices.

416
00:42:13,080 --> 00:42:15,839
Nayman.

417
00:42:16,400 --> 00:42:18,599
Oh souls, salute Nayman!

418
00:42:18,600 --> 00:42:20,119
Oh souls, salute Nayman!

419
00:42:20,120 --> 00:42:22,599
Oh souls, salute Nayman!

420
00:42:34,080 --> 00:42:40,359
Oh souls, salute Nayman.

421
00:42:45,600 --> 00:42:48,489
Nayman, the greatest!

422
00:42:48,640 --> 00:42:51,679
Nayman, the greatest!

423
00:43:02,000 --> 00:43:05,959
The souls are greeting the greatest
Nayman, sir.

424
00:43:06,360 --> 00:43:08,479
Nayman, the greatest!

425
00:43:09,080 --> 00:43:12,399
Nayman, the greatest!

426
00:43:16,280 --> 00:43:18,199
Nayman, the greatest!

427
00:43:18,800 --> 00:43:20,799
Nayman, the greatest!

428
00:43:24,000 --> 00:43:26,199
I made the night sleep 15 times!

429
00:43:26,480 --> 00:43:29,279
I made the sun go mad 15 times!

430
00:43:30,440 --> 00:43:32,239
For what?

431
00:43:33,440 --> 00:43:34,919
For today!

432
00:43:38,400 --> 00:43:40,439
Where are the Beys?

433
00:43:41,600 --> 00:43:45,799
They are on their ways, Nayman.
They will be here for the council.

434
00:43:46,120 --> 00:43:48,359
Those who can't make it in time...

435
00:43:48,760 --> 00:43:50,959
will die.

436
00:43:51,320 --> 00:43:53,679
They will either stand with me...

437
00:43:54,080 --> 00:43:57,359
or they will die!

438
00:44:05,160 --> 00:44:06,519
Kutan.

439
00:44:08,200 --> 00:44:09,639
Acar.

440
00:44:12,280 --> 00:44:14,599
You can rest easy.

441
00:44:17,920 --> 00:44:21,719
I am going to kill all of
them with my hands.

442
00:44:24,200 --> 00:44:27,399
Then I will meet you.

443
00:44:28,720 --> 00:44:30,959
You can rest easy.

444
00:44:37,360 --> 00:44:39,639
What's the situation
in Yenişehir, tell me.

445
00:44:40,080 --> 00:44:43,039
The construction for the soup
kitchen began, my Bey.

446
00:44:44,720 --> 00:44:50,109
Until aunt Bala's wounds heal, Alçiçek
will take care of the soup kitchen.

447
00:44:51,280 --> 00:44:54,399
Many people come and ask for
our help every day. Thank Allah.

448
00:44:54,600 --> 00:44:56,679
This soup kitchen is important.

449
00:44:57,640 --> 00:45:01,279
Alçiçek took responsibility in my absence.

450
00:45:01,400 --> 00:45:05,719
But my wounds are healed now, I
will return back to the work quickly.

451
00:45:05,840 --> 00:45:08,359
Alçiçek must be tired.

452
00:45:08,440 --> 00:45:09,399
No.

453
00:45:09,720 --> 00:45:12,999
A blessed duty like this
wouldn't tire any of us.

454
00:45:13,400 --> 00:45:14,999
No.

455
00:45:16,200 --> 00:45:18,319
The people matters more.

456
00:45:19,000 --> 00:45:23,759
That's why, Alçiçek will stay at the
soup kitchen for a little longer.

457
00:45:26,000 --> 00:45:26,599
Bala.

458
00:45:28,360 --> 00:45:30,159
You have another duty.

459
00:45:31,480 --> 00:45:33,279
Yes, my Bey.

460
00:45:41,320 --> 00:45:43,879
They are surrounding us from all sides.

461
00:45:47,400 --> 00:45:50,319
We will not wait here or outside.

462
00:45:51,600 --> 00:45:53,679
We will always walk forward.

463
00:45:57,000 --> 00:45:58,999
What about Turgut Bey?

464
00:46:02,520 --> 00:46:08,199
Nayman thinks that we
will stop because he has Turgut.

465
00:46:10,640 --> 00:46:12,959
And until the time he has given us comes...

466
00:46:13,400 --> 00:46:15,399
he won't do anything.

467
00:46:16,720 --> 00:46:18,319
We will save Turgut.

468
00:46:19,760 --> 00:46:21,039
Now tell me.

469
00:46:22,240 --> 00:46:23,959
How are the preparations in Yenişehir?

470
00:46:24,000 --> 00:46:26,199
We took precautions in Yenişehir, Osman Bey.

471
00:46:26,200 --> 00:46:29,359
But the enemy is still inside.

472
00:46:30,000 --> 00:46:32,239
What are we going to do against İsmihan?

473
00:46:32,640 --> 00:46:35,519
The real question is what will Ismihan do.

474
00:46:35,920 --> 00:46:38,399
What if he stops the
army that will come here?

475
00:46:39,960 --> 00:46:42,919
We know İsmihan is in Konya now.

476
00:46:44,600 --> 00:46:47,199
As long as Sultan Alaaddin
sits on the throne...

477
00:46:48,560 --> 00:46:50,799
we can't do anything.

478
00:46:54,320 --> 00:46:56,279
Maybe that's what she wants.

479
00:46:58,120 --> 00:46:59,719
They still have time.

480
00:47:12,800 --> 00:47:14,919
How could you do that, mother?

481
00:47:16,280 --> 00:47:18,279
How could you give the seal to him?

482
00:47:18,280 --> 00:47:21,719
Aren't you worried about
the future of our land?

483
00:47:22,400 --> 00:47:24,199
I gave it because I care about it!

484
00:47:24,520 --> 00:47:25,999
Is this how you care?

485
00:47:26,320 --> 00:47:30,599
By giving unlimited power to Nayman?

486
00:47:30,840 --> 00:47:33,879
There is no other option
to get rid of Osman

487
00:47:34,040 --> 00:47:35,519
I can't understand.

488
00:47:35,720 --> 00:47:40,039
I can't understand it! We are
on the same side with Osman.

489
00:47:41,000 --> 00:47:45,799
How can we be on the same side as
a rebellious Bey who wants to be free?

490
00:47:50,480 --> 00:47:53,559
Nayman is an enemy!

491
00:47:54,200 --> 00:47:58,239
But Osman is a traitor, Alaaddin.

492
00:48:02,000 --> 00:48:03,479
When Nayrnan...

493
00:48:04,400 --> 00:48:07,399
removes Osman from these lands...

494
00:48:07,720 --> 00:48:09,399
he will leave.

495
00:48:10,360 --> 00:48:14,999
He will give Konya and the borders to us.

496
00:48:15,640 --> 00:48:17,119
That's what'we agreed on.

497
00:48:21,200 --> 00:48:22,439
Mother.

498
00:48:23,720 --> 00:48:25,439
How can you trust a Mongolian?

499
00:48:25,440 --> 00:48:27,119
I don't trust anyone.

500
00:48:28,960 --> 00:48:32,639
Nayman is going to destroy
Osman with that seal!

501
00:48:33,720 --> 00:48:37,039
Then, he will go after Gazan.

502
00:48:37,280 --> 00:48:42,439
As they're destroying each other,
we'll be the most powerful in these lands.

503
00:48:44,240 --> 00:48:47,759
For our future, there
is no other way.

504
00:49:50,040 --> 00:49:53,259
With the power of immortal God...

505
00:49:53,680 --> 00:49:57,879
those who are destined
with the world dominance!

506
00:49:59,000 --> 00:50:01,199
Let the council begin.

507
00:50:10,800 --> 00:50:14,079
First, we will swear an oath.

508
00:50:18,480 --> 00:50:24,999
Without swearing an oath,
there can't be a council.

509
00:50:27,920 --> 00:50:30,119
Our blood will be mixed.

510
00:50:30,520 --> 00:50:32,399
We will swear an oath.

511
00:50:32,800 --> 00:50:35,239
It will be mixed.

512
00:50:35,600 --> 00:50:38,879
And the blood will be drunk!

513
00:51:06,680 --> 00:51:09,809
Our freedom...

514
00:51:12,480 --> 00:51:14,439
is in Nayman's command.

515
00:51:33,360 --> 00:51:35,039
Our sword..

516
00:51:38,520 --> 00:51:40,639
is held by Nayman!

517
00:51:55,240 --> 00:51:59,199
Our fate is in Nayman's hands!

518
00:52:03,600 --> 00:52:06,759
Our fate is in Nayman's hands!

519
00:52:28,280 --> 00:52:32,799
Drinking this to destroy
those who stand against us!

520
00:52:41,760 --> 00:52:43,319
Drinking...

521
00:52:43,320 --> 00:52:48,599
this to move Cengiz's legacy further.

522
00:53:14,440 --> 00:53:19,359
This legacy which goes
from China to Byzantine.

523
00:53:20,760 --> 00:53:25,999
We won't leave it to
those who are in betrayal.

524
00:53:26,000 --> 00:53:29,319
From Tebriz, Karakurum..

525
00:53:29,320 --> 00:53:32,119
Hanbalık you have come from.

526
00:53:35,000 --> 00:53:38,679
We swore and saw the seal.

527
00:53:39,760 --> 00:53:41,199
Now...

528
00:53:41,200 --> 00:53:44,159
our soldiers who
have been waiting can come.

529
00:53:44,160 --> 00:53:45,639
Tendağ.

530
00:53:48,000 --> 00:53:50,119
Send the messengers.

531
00:53:54,920 --> 00:54:02,119
This world has been created by
the Sky Tengri (God) for the strong to rule.

532
00:54:03,160 --> 00:54:05,599
There are small bugs...

533
00:54:05,600 --> 00:54:08,159
like Osman.

534
00:54:09,000 --> 00:54:13,119
We will end them for those who
might get the wrong idea.

535
00:54:13,360 --> 00:54:21,309
Mongolian chanting

536
00:54:22,120 --> 00:54:24,519
My Bey, there's word.

537
00:54:24,520 --> 00:54:26,799
Thank you.

538
00:54:32,480 --> 00:54:35,359
It's about the Beys who
went to Nayman's invitation.

539
00:54:36,600 --> 00:54:39,519
They reached Nayman's
headquarters.

540
00:54:40,120 --> 00:54:43,239
And they went there with
a lot of presents too.

541
00:54:44,800 --> 00:54:47,319
Those are for Nayman.

542
00:54:50,880 --> 00:54:53,799
They want to get close to him.

543
00:54:55,880 --> 00:54:56,639
But..

544
00:54:58,520 --> 00:55:01,279
But their army won't be with them.

545
00:55:01,640 --> 00:55:03,959
Why is the reason, my Bey?

546
00:55:06,360 --> 00:55:09,919
They want to decide about
the army during the council.

547
00:55:09,920 --> 00:55:12,119
If the order is ruled...

548
00:55:12,120 --> 00:55:13,719
then...

549
00:55:13,720 --> 00:55:16,279
they will send messengers
to the commanders.

550
00:55:19,200 --> 00:55:21,359
What they are intending is...

551
00:55:21,780 --> 00:55:24,859
to see if the seal is real or not.

552
00:55:26,600 --> 00:55:29,599
Who will be their commanders?

553
00:55:31,080 --> 00:55:33,919
Nayman is after a
strong move right now.

554
00:55:34,600 --> 00:55:36,119
Those commanders...

555
00:55:36,840 --> 00:55:40,399
have the same blood as
the ones at the council.

556
00:55:43,280 --> 00:55:44,999
Either their son...

557
00:55:45,000 --> 00:55:46,959
or son in law...

558
00:55:46,960 --> 00:55:48,519
or their niece.

559
00:55:50,920 --> 00:55:54,759
Nayman is preparing a move that
will go on for years.

560
00:55:55,160 --> 00:55:56,599
That's why...

561
00:55:58,000 --> 00:56:00,439
he's collecting...

562
00:56:01,160 --> 00:56:03,999
those who are the strongest
without caring for their ages.

563
00:56:05,520 --> 00:56:07,159
But we won't..

564
00:56:08,280 --> 00:56:11,919
let the messengers pass.

565
00:56:14,400 --> 00:56:16,879
If they do...

566
00:56:17,440 --> 00:56:20,079
if the army comes...

567
00:56:20,400 --> 00:56:22,679
we can't get Turgut...

568
00:56:23,800 --> 00:56:25,719
or stay free.

569
00:56:26,480 --> 00:56:28,199
Your command, my bey.

570
00:56:28,480 --> 00:56:30,199
May I come in, my Bey?

571
00:56:31,400 --> 00:56:32,919
Come in.

572
00:56:36,600 --> 00:56:37,799
My Bey.

573
00:56:37,800 --> 00:56:39,999
There is a word from the Alps.

574
00:56:40,000 --> 00:56:40,919
As you said...

575
00:56:41,040 --> 00:56:43,519
he council sent the messengers away.

576
00:56:54,840 --> 00:56:57,119
Everyone will go
to their posts.

577
00:56:57,120 --> 00:56:59,119
Come on, Alps.

578
00:57:11,000 --> 00:57:12,999
The armies will be here.

579
00:57:13,000 --> 00:57:15,519
But there will be people
who will stand against you.

580
00:57:16,120 --> 00:57:19,119
What will be your move
against them, Nayman?

581
00:57:19,120 --> 00:57:20,999
When....

582
00:57:21,000 --> 00:57:23,199
Cengiz Khan's seal is in my hands...

583
00:57:23,200 --> 00:57:26,599
everyone who goes
against me is a traitor.

584
00:57:27,360 --> 00:57:29,439
When the armies come..

585
00:57:29,440 --> 00:57:32,319
I’m going to declare
myself as the Khan.

586
00:57:32,320 --> 00:57:36,119
I'm going to make those who
got off the path get back on it.

587
00:57:36,320 --> 00:57:38,919
I'm going to destroy those who...

588
00:57:38,920 --> 00:57:42,799
try to stop us.

589
00:57:43,400 --> 00:57:44,959
Who are those?

590
00:57:45,760 --> 00:57:48,319
Muslims.

591
00:57:48,760 --> 00:57:51,639
They tricked people.

592
00:57:51,640 --> 00:57:54,079
The people of the nation...

593
00:57:54,080 --> 00:57:56,919
are choosing Islam day by day.

594
00:57:57,480 --> 00:58:02,399
The commanders in Konya
are choosing Islam.

595
00:58:03,720 --> 00:58:06,159
They're disappearing.

596
00:58:06,160 --> 00:58:11,639
Sky Tengri is leaving us
slowly because of them.

597
00:58:15,400 --> 00:58:17,719
Under my Khanate...

598
00:58:17,720 --> 00:58:20,919
not one of them will live.

599
00:58:20,920 --> 00:58:24,639
We will be reborn
with your rule.

600
00:58:30,200 --> 00:58:31,159
Shaman.

601
00:58:31,440 --> 00:58:34,199
Throw the bones in the fire.

602
00:58:35,000 --> 00:58:37,519
Let the fire show us...

603
00:58:37,520 --> 00:58:42,559
who will come victorious out of this war.

604
00:59:24,640 --> 00:59:25,639
It's either now..

605
00:59:26,120 --> 00:59:29,039
or never, Cerkutay.

606
00:59:36,280 --> 00:59:38,759
Cerkutay?

607
00:59:40,000 --> 00:59:41,799
Are you hungry?

608
00:59:42,000 --> 00:59:44,719
You need to wait a little.

609
00:59:44,960 --> 00:59:47,639
There's no time to wait, Ülgen.

610
00:59:48,200 --> 00:59:49,719
There's no time.

611
00:59:51,560 --> 00:59:53,919
I will make you something else then.

612
00:59:54,480 --> 00:59:55,999
It’s not that.

613
00:59:56,600 --> 00:59:58,159
There's just no time.

614
01:00:03,280 --> 01:00:05,519
Ülgen...

615
01:00:10,880 --> 01:00:14,799
do you know what I first thought of...

616
01:00:15,560 --> 01:00:18,679
when I saw the palace in fires?

617
01:00:22,080 --> 01:00:23,799
What was it?

618
01:00:26,600 --> 01:00:28,399
It was you.

619
01:00:31,200 --> 01:00:33,399
I wondered where you were...

620
01:00:33,800 --> 01:00:36,359
and how you were doing.

621
01:00:38,800 --> 01:00:40,399
My heart was aching.

622
01:00:40,600 --> 01:00:42,919
- Cerkutay...--
- Wait, Ülgen.

623
01:00:44,480 --> 01:00:48,039
I've been meaning to say
these things for a long time...

624
01:00:48,400 --> 01:00:50,559
so while I'm at it...

625
01:00:50,920 --> 01:00:52,639
let me speak.

626
01:01:00,240 --> 01:01:03,039
You know, I had buried my
heart under the dirt.

627
01:01:05,040 --> 01:01:09,119
But you pulled it back out.

628
01:01:21,400 --> 01:01:24,079
I'm in love with you, Ülgen.

629
01:01:47,800 --> 01:01:49,599
Ülgen?

630
01:01:52,720 --> 01:01:54,839
Ülgen...

631
01:01:58,000 --> 01:01:59,519
Ülgen!

632
01:02:00,160 --> 01:02:01,919
Ülgen!

633
01:02:04,640 --> 01:02:06,319
Ülgen!

634
01:02:07,840 --> 01:02:10,999
Oh no, it’s the dark midwife!

635
01:02:11,400 --> 01:02:13,599
Where are you, Ülgen?

636
01:02:16,240 --> 01:02:17,999
Ülgen!

637
01:02:19,280 --> 01:02:20,199
Girl...

638
01:02:20,280 --> 01:02:21,999
Ülgen!

639
01:02:22,320 --> 01:02:23,799
Girl!

640
01:02:28,560 --> 01:02:29,559
Are you okay?

641
01:02:31,480 --> 01:02:34,879
I'm in love with you, too.

642
01:02:36,010 --> 01:02:37,129
What?

643
01:02:37,480 --> 01:02:38,079
Get up!

644
01:02:44,080 --> 01:02:45,999
You're in love, huh?

645
01:02:48,880 --> 01:02:50,239
Mother?

646
01:02:51,600 --> 01:02:53,639
Yes!

647
01:02:57,040 --> 01:02:59,959
I must have fallen asleep.

648
01:03:02,320 --> 01:03:05,959
Thousands of soldiers are waiting on
your command, Nayman the Great.

649
01:03:06,240 --> 01:03:08,879
The Shaman pointed out
to a victory!

650
01:03:09,120 --> 01:03:11,879
Why don't we destroy
Yenişehir right now?

651
01:03:12,000 --> 01:03:16,919
Osman is making Yenişehir
a strong castle.

652
01:03:17,520 --> 01:03:19,759
He's being very careful.

653
01:03:22,040 --> 01:03:26,399
Do you think we'll lose more than
what we'll win?

654
01:03:27,160 --> 01:03:32,199
I will not send the soldiers there
before the army arrives.

655
01:03:33,360 --> 01:03:37,399
Once the army is here, not only
we'll destroy Yenişehir...

656
01:03:37,760 --> 01:03:42,039
but we will also bring
chaos to all their lands!

657
01:03:43,440 --> 01:03:45,439
Is it just Osman?

658
01:03:45,600 --> 01:03:49,599
You're not easily satisfied...

659
01:03:49,920 --> 01:03:51,719
are you?

660
01:03:52,080 --> 01:03:55,879
The army will march on the Byzantines...

661
01:03:56,800 --> 01:04:00,279
and destroy all other Beys as well.

662
01:04:00,720 --> 01:04:02,159
Then, what?

663
01:04:02,560 --> 01:04:04,359
We already know what we'll win...

664
01:04:04,720 --> 01:04:07,439
Slaves, maidens...

665
01:04:08,320 --> 01:04:10,799
and lots of spoils.

666
01:04:14,200 --> 01:04:16,479
After the war...

667
01:04:16,680 --> 01:04:19,319
we will march towards Tebriz and Gazhan!

668
01:04:20,000 --> 01:04:21,719
Then...

669
01:04:22,080 --> 01:04:24,479
we'll set out for the whole world!

670
01:04:24,720 --> 01:04:27,159
The whole world!

671
01:04:29,000 --> 01:04:31,759
Can I come in, Mother Sultan?

672
01:04:35,560 --> 01:04:37,599
Come in, Bayındır.

673
01:04:47,320 --> 01:04:49,759
Mother Sultan.

674
01:04:50,120 --> 01:04:53,599
We've made all
preparations for the road.

675
01:04:53,880 --> 01:04:57,159
We're ready.

676
01:04:57,840 --> 01:05:00,679
Did you check twice, Bayindir?

677
01:05:03,920 --> 01:05:05,399
You know...

678
01:05:05,680 --> 01:05:07,319
you haven’t done anything right...

679
01:05:08,200 --> 01:05:11,399
since your failure at the palace.

680
01:05:11,800 --> 01:05:14,639
Mother Sultan...

681
01:05:14,640 --> 01:05:19,639
hearing you speak like that
makes me wish that...

682
01:05:20,160 --> 01:05:22,599
I was dead along with those soldiers.

683
01:05:22,680 --> 01:05:25,119
- When Osman Bey came...--
- Shut up!

684
01:05:29,240 --> 01:05:30,879
You're unskilled...

685
01:05:31,600 --> 01:05:33,719
yet you're smart.

686
01:05:34,800 --> 01:05:39,239
You know when to switch your side
once you realize it won't end well.

687
01:05:41,200 --> 01:05:43,359
Mother Sultan...

688
01:05:43,480 --> 01:05:46,999
you can trust your humble servant Bayindir.

689
01:05:47,400 --> 01:05:50,279
I'm always on your side.

690
01:05:51,000 --> 01:05:53,599
However...

691
01:05:54,080 --> 01:05:57,159
about Nayman's council...

692
01:05:59,000 --> 01:06:02,679
What do you mean, Bayindir?

693
01:06:06,840 --> 01:06:11,759
Mother Sultan, I don't
trust that infidel...

694
01:06:12,840 --> 01:06:15,239
Nayman.

695
01:06:16,240 --> 01:06:17,559
I wonder...

696
01:06:18,800 --> 01:06:21,199
if there is a trick behind this.

697
01:06:45,880 --> 01:06:49,719
I will side with them.

698
01:06:50,120 --> 01:06:52,639
Why are you mad, my Bey?
Did something happen?

699
01:06:52,800 --> 01:06:56,759
From now on, I will side with the
ones that follow Allah's path.

700
01:07:02,240 --> 01:07:06,599
Let's see if we can stop Ismihan before...

701
01:07:07,160 --> 01:07:09,959
she reaches the council.

702
01:07:12,000 --> 01:07:14,759
So, Mother Sultan plays a game, huh?

703
01:07:16,400 --> 01:07:19,199
Are we going to make a
plan against them, my Bey?

704
01:07:20,920 --> 01:07:22,599
So...

705
01:07:29,800 --> 01:07:34,599
I don't trust you, Bayindir.

706
01:07:35,600 --> 01:07:37,019
You should know that.

707
01:07:37,600 --> 01:07:39,839
I would never trust you.

708
01:07:41,240 --> 01:07:42,639
Now...

709
01:07:43,920 --> 01:07:46,119
with your smallest mistake...

710
01:07:48,560 --> 01:07:50,319
my sword will fall onto your neck.

711
01:07:51,800 --> 01:07:53,959
I will sacrifice my
life for you, my Bey.

712
01:07:55,080 --> 01:08:01,639
May Allah grant me martyrdom
while fighting for you.

713
01:08:04,600 --> 01:08:06,919
I repented for my sins, my Bey.

714
01:08:09,160 --> 01:08:15,479
From now on, I will not play any trick
against anyone that is not an infidel.

715
01:08:16,160 --> 01:08:17,679
We will see.

716
01:08:19,399 --> 01:08:21,799
We will live and see.

717
01:08:24,680 --> 01:08:27,158
Now, you will go to Mother Sultan.

718
01:08:29,160 --> 01:08:31,678
You will make her and
Nayman fight each other.

719
01:08:32,240 --> 01:08:34,037
When they are weakened..

720
01:08:35,000 --> 01:08:36,879
I will take care of the rest.

721
01:08:38,439 --> 01:08:39,519
Come on.

722
01:08:43,439 --> 01:08:46,999
My Bey, what was the reason
for that slap?

723
01:08:54,200 --> 01:08:56,759
For what you have done!

724
01:08:57,439 --> 01:08:58,399
Leave!

725
01:08:58,399 --> 01:09:00,198
Your command, my Bey.

726
01:09:05,399 --> 01:09:08,399
Send word to Osman Bey quickly.

727
01:09:09,000 --> 01:09:13,399
İssmihan stopped the army that
was going to leave Konya.

728
01:09:14,840 --> 01:09:16,799
We are returning to Söğüt now.

729
01:09:18,399 --> 01:09:19,479
Come on.

730
01:09:35,600 --> 01:09:37,238
Brother, they are coming.

731
01:09:37,399 --> 01:09:38,959
I heard it, brother.

732
01:09:38,960 --> 01:09:40,479
We will not let anyone pass.

733
01:09:40,479 --> 01:09:41,759
Okay.

734
01:09:46,720 --> 01:09:50,078
Stop, warriors!

735
01:09:52,880 --> 01:09:56,159
Who can stop Nayman's messenger?

736
01:09:57,120 --> 01:10:00,879
Well, not me, brother, it's Osman
Bey's orders.

737
01:10:19,600 --> 01:10:20,799
It was a clean job, huh, brother?

738
01:10:21,040 --> 01:10:22,159
Thank Allah.

739
01:10:28,720 --> 01:10:30,399
What's written on it?

740
01:10:30,400 --> 01:10:31,919
What's that brother?

741
01:10:56,600 --> 01:10:57,759
To the horses.

742
01:11:36,320 --> 01:11:38,679
Stop!

743
01:11:38,680 --> 01:11:39,599
What do you want?

744
01:11:39,600 --> 01:11:40,759
Stop there.

745
01:11:47,360 --> 01:11:48,799
Where are you going?

746
01:11:56,640 --> 01:12:00,519
Are you carrying a message from Nayman?

747
01:12:35,560 --> 01:12:37,919
Nayman took precaution.

748
01:12:38,200 --> 01:12:39,919
How did you understand, brother?

749
01:12:42,000 --> 01:12:46,399
The letter the messenger was carrying
was empty. This is the real letter.

750
01:12:49,160 --> 01:12:53,799
The route of the Beys from
the council is written on it.

751
01:12:55,800 --> 01:12:58,519
Turahan, send word to Alps.

752
01:12:58,680 --> 01:13:03,599
Tell them not to allow any
merchant carriages or villagers to leave.

753
01:13:20,920 --> 01:13:23,639
Mother Sultan...

754
01:13:23,640 --> 01:13:25,959
you thought so well.

755
01:13:26,760 --> 01:13:31,439
If Sultan Alaaddin doesn't send an army..

756
01:13:31,440 --> 01:13:35,359
Osman will have a hard time.

757
01:13:36,360 --> 01:13:37,519
But...

758
01:13:38,800 --> 01:13:42,559
when he learns that you've done this...

759
01:13:42,560 --> 01:13:45,399
he will attack you with everything he has.

760
01:13:45,400 --> 01:13:46,719
No.

761
01:13:47,440 --> 01:13:50,239
Nayman has weakened Osman.

762
01:13:50,240 --> 01:13:54,759
Osman doesn’t have the strength for
another fight.

763
01:13:54,760 --> 01:13:58,639
He knows that he will
lose his head if he rebels.

764
01:13:58,640 --> 01:14:02,399
The only thing he doesn't know is
that Nayman and I are on the same side.

765
01:14:02,400 --> 01:14:03,999
And that will lead us to victory.

766
01:14:05,520 --> 01:14:10,559
Betrayal to Seljuk won't
be looked over.

767
01:14:11,000 --> 01:14:12,919
But...

768
01:14:12,920 --> 01:14:18,159
can we trust Nayman, Mother Sultan?

769
01:14:18,800 --> 01:14:23,679
A commander who wants to
rule over the world...

770
01:14:23,680 --> 01:14:27,519
Why would he let you get stronger?

771
01:14:27,520 --> 01:14:30,559
We have the same goal
with Nayman, Bayındır.

772
01:14:32,360 --> 01:14:36,199
We agreed to destroy Osman.

773
01:14:36,200 --> 01:14:38,599
He will stay loyal to it.

774
01:14:38,600 --> 01:14:44,159
You know the best but we
still need to be careful.

775
01:14:44,160 --> 01:14:46,199
Nayman feeds on blood.

776
01:14:46,200 --> 01:14:49,519
When Osman falls, may Allah forbid...

777
01:14:50,280 --> 01:14:52,199
he might turn towards you.

778
01:14:59,800 --> 01:15:02,999
I decide on the target, Bayindir.

779
01:15:03,920 --> 01:15:06,199
Both Osman and Nayman will be destroyed.

780
01:15:06,640 --> 01:15:09,799
The ruler of these lands...

781
01:15:13,120 --> 01:15:14,639
will be me.

782
01:15:16,200 --> 01:15:18,679
Come on.

783
01:15:34,880 --> 01:15:39,239
The relatives of the Mongol
Beys will come with a big army.

784
01:15:41,000 --> 01:15:44,439
He wants them to come without resting.

785
01:15:45,920 --> 01:15:47,679
Then...

786
01:15:48,680 --> 01:15:52,199
we will make them our guests in a inn.

787
01:15:53,600 --> 01:15:57,159
An army without its commander
can’t move.

788
01:15:57,160 --> 01:16:00,719
We'll capture the relatives of the
Mongol Beys in the caravanserai.

789
01:16:01,040 --> 01:16:05,199
I would let them go under one condition.

790
01:16:06,920 --> 01:16:09,519
They will leave our lands.

791
01:16:11,040 --> 01:16:12,759
The seal unites them.

792
01:16:13,360 --> 01:16:15,159
But we will stop that.

793
01:16:15,680 --> 01:16:18,879
They will get out of our lands.

794
01:16:24,320 --> 01:16:28,519
If they don't give Turgut Bey
in exchange for them...

795
01:16:29,680 --> 01:16:33,319
...I'm going to kill them
in front of their relatives.

796
01:16:37,280 --> 01:16:38,159
My bey.

797
01:16:39,000 --> 01:16:40,839
Change the compass.

798
01:16:41,360 --> 01:16:44,719
Their commanders will enter
the in from Ingoz route.

799
01:16:44,720 --> 01:16:46,359
As you wish my bey.

800
01:16:46,360 --> 01:16:48,399
Now everyone goes back to their job.

801
01:16:48,400 --> 01:16:50,199
As you wish my bey.

802
01:16:50,200 --> 01:16:51,159
Come on.

803
01:16:53,880 --> 01:16:55,119
My bey.

804
01:16:55,120 --> 01:16:58,559
My bey that's Mongol's military inn.

805
01:16:58,960 --> 01:17:01,399
They won't believe it otherwise.

806
01:17:01,400 --> 01:17:03,599
We will go to the inn beforehand...

807
01:17:03,600 --> 01:17:05,719
...and take it.

808
01:17:05,720 --> 01:17:08,399
And we are going to welcome them.

809
01:17:08,800 --> 01:17:10,559
Tell me about the inn.

810
01:17:10,920 --> 01:17:12,559
As you wish my Bey.

811
01:17:13,080 --> 01:17:13,999
My Bey.

812
01:17:18,720 --> 01:17:20,039
Come on.

813
01:17:22,880 --> 01:17:24,439
Who are you?

814
01:17:25,600 --> 01:17:26,799
I'm...

815
01:17:28,240 --> 01:17:30,399
...Cerkut Tay.

816
01:17:31,120 --> 01:17:32,759
And this is my slave.

817
01:17:33,480 --> 01:17:35,119
You enslaved a Turk, huh?

818
01:17:36,320 --> 01:17:38,879
Good job, good job.

819
01:17:44,080 --> 01:17:46,799
Let me give you a tip, soldier.

820
01:17:57,960 --> 01:17:59,639
A Turk can never be enslaved.

821
01:18:56,000 --> 01:18:57,599
The commanders..

822
01:18:57,600 --> 01:19:01,199
...are coming to our lands to spill blood.

823
01:19:01,720 --> 01:19:04,319
Their armies are deployed in the valley.

824
01:19:04,320 --> 01:19:05,999
Let them come.

825
01:19:06,000 --> 01:19:07,719
Let them.

826
01:19:07,720 --> 01:19:10,599
We will show them how hospitable we are.

827
01:19:11,240 --> 01:19:13,359
We'll cook.

828
01:19:13,360 --> 01:19:14,719
Alps.

829
01:19:14,840 --> 01:19:17,399
Everyone go to their jobs!

830
01:19:17,400 --> 01:19:18,959
As you wish my Bey!

831
01:19:18,960 --> 01:19:20,439
Come on.

832
01:19:24,360 --> 01:19:26,319
Let them come.

833
01:19:26,960 --> 01:19:28,399
Let them.

834
01:19:29,920 --> 01:19:30,799
Bala.

835
01:19:33,920 --> 01:19:35,919
Let's go.

836
01:19:39,960 --> 01:19:43,399
Welcome, royal commanders.

837
01:19:49,680 --> 01:19:52,799
Welcome, mighty commanders.

838
01:20:09,400 --> 01:20:11,399
Eat well.

839
01:20:11,520 --> 01:20:14,479
Once Nayman and our ancestors start the war...

840
01:20:14,960 --> 01:20:16,559
...we will have no time to eat or rest.

841
01:20:16,960 --> 01:20:19,119
Keep eating.

842
01:20:19,600 --> 01:20:21,599
We'll sip on Turk blood after our meals!

843
01:20:28,440 --> 01:20:30,519
Who are you?

844
01:20:32,000 --> 01:20:35,639
Don't you know no one is allowed here
while the commanders are coming?

845
01:20:53,360 --> 01:20:55,639
Where are you going?

846
01:20:56,000 --> 01:20:57,199
To the battle!

847
01:20:57,400 --> 01:21:00,319
To make mountains out of Turks' bones.

848
01:21:00,480 --> 01:21:02,759
To drink their blood!

849
01:21:03,280 --> 01:21:05,519
Who's in the lead?

850
01:21:05,720 --> 01:21:08,599
Someone called Osman Bey

851
01:21:10,240 --> 01:21:12,079
You're looking at him.

852
01:21:14,920 --> 01:21:16,519
Are you Osman?

853
01:21:16,720 --> 01:21:17,879
I am.

854
01:21:17,880 --> 01:21:19,799
We were looking for you, Osman.

855
01:21:32,800 --> 01:21:33,799
Behold!

856
01:21:34,080 --> 01:21:38,199
Stay put if you want him to keep his head!

857
01:21:40,520 --> 01:21:43,719
Even hundreds of you...

858
01:21:44,200 --> 01:21:47,159
...are still no match for Turgut only.

859
01:21:48,080 --> 01:21:50,199
You may keep breathing until...

860
01:21:50,560 --> 01:21:53,159
...the council is disbanded...

861
01:21:54,400 --> 01:21:56,319
...and Turgut is back.

862
01:21:56,400 --> 01:22:01,079
We were on our way to kill you but
you welcomed us on the way, Osman

863
01:22:01,560 --> 01:22:02,799
You will die!

864
01:22:02,920 --> 01:22:05,279
As long as our base is still there..

865
01:22:05,520 --> 01:22:08,199
...you, your Alps...

866
01:22:08,400 --> 01:22:11,919
...and that Hatun of yours-

867
01:22:25,200 --> 01:22:29,999
You don't know anything about the land
you're going after...

868
01:22:31,200 --> 01:22:32,839
This is the land of Muslims...

869
01:22:33,560 --> 01:22:35,839
The land of Turks!

870
01:22:37,720 --> 01:22:39,239
You may enter...

871
01:22:39,960 --> 01:22:41,399
...however...

872
01:22:42,200 --> 01:22:45,199
...you can't leave before you die.

873
01:22:51,400 --> 01:22:53,679
Even if it takes centuries..

874
01:22:54,800 --> 01:22:57,439
...we will make sure you acknowledge that.

875
01:23:57,400 --> 01:23:59,199
Bring him!

876
01:24:02,440 --> 01:24:03,839
You can leave.

877
01:24:11,560 --> 01:24:14,999
You're here because you thought...

878
01:24:15,520 --> 01:24:18,439
...you had what it takes to face me, Turgut.

879
01:24:20,480 --> 01:24:22,879
But you lost.

880
01:24:25,680 --> 01:24:29,999
You will witness the great state
I am about to found.

881
01:24:31,560 --> 01:24:33,279
The dream you always have for...

882
01:24:33,920 --> 01:24:37,399
...ruling the whole world...

883
01:24:41,200 --> 01:24:43,799
...will be the end of the Mongols.

884
01:24:47,080 --> 01:24:49,839
But your end...

885
01:24:50,120 --> 01:24:54,599
...will be by the hand of my brother,
Osman Bey!

886
01:24:59,480 --> 01:25:02,159
No one can stop me...

887
01:25:02,560 --> 01:25:06,159
...as long as I have this seal.

888
01:25:10,320 --> 01:25:13,119
I know the sea

889
01:25:13,400 --> 01:25:17,239
I once possessed it

890
01:25:19,040 --> 01:25:23,279
I took it by personally cutting your
brothers throat.

891
01:25:27,720 --> 01:25:30,079
Was it Talay?

892
01:25:33,080 --> 01:25:35,279
Talay...

893
01:25:36,120 --> 01:25:38,799
Your efforts to get yourself killed...

894
01:25:39,040 --> 01:25:41,199
...are in vain.

895
01:25:41,520 --> 01:25:44,599
I killed your Alps, remember?

896
01:25:48,000 --> 01:25:50,719
My army is on it's way.

897
01:25:51,080 --> 01:25:55,199
I will make Inegol my stable

898
01:25:55,600 --> 01:25:57,919
My stable!

899
01:26:00,800 --> 01:26:02,559
We'll see...

900
01:26:03,320 --> 01:26:06,079
..what fate has in store for us.

901
01:26:10,720 --> 01:26:13,639
What now, Osman?

902
01:26:18,760 --> 01:26:20,439
Alps...

903
01:26:20,840 --> 01:26:22,839
...you, too, might be wondering...

904
01:26:23,000 --> 01:26:25,359
...how we're going to go to
Nayman's council...

905
01:26:25,520 --> 01:26:28,199
...with the Mongolian army
standing outside.

906
01:26:28,680 --> 01:26:31,479
He who had a plan to get in...

907
01:26:32,360 --> 01:26:34,319
...must have a way out as well, my Bey.

908
01:26:34,319 --> 01:26:36,239
Of course I do.

909
01:26:37,200 --> 01:26:39,479
-Cerkutay.
-My Bey.

910
01:26:43,120 --> 01:26:44,839
Here..

911
01:26:45,320 --> 01:26:47,799
...is a letter that says
the army isn't needed...

912
01:26:47,799 --> 01:26:51,839
...and the forces are to
return to their posts.

913
01:26:52,600 --> 01:26:53,879
Now...

914
01:26:54,080 --> 01:26:56,599
...all commanders will put
their seals under it.

915
01:26:56,800 --> 01:26:58,399
If they don't...

916
01:26:58,560 --> 01:27:01,359
...we will kill them.

917
01:27:03,960 --> 01:27:05,159
My Bey.

918
01:27:07,240 --> 01:27:09,599
Do you think they will believe me?

919
01:27:11,800 --> 01:27:13,719
They will.

920
01:27:14,240 --> 01:27:16,639
Of course they wi

921
01:27:36,400 --> 01:27:41,639
Do you see that one?
You will go there as his aide.

922
01:27:42,560 --> 01:27:45,599
You will keep your dagger on his back.

923
01:27:46,600 --> 01:27:48,479
He will give the letter to the army.

924
01:27:48,720 --> 01:27:52,159
If he tries anything, cut his
head in front of the army.

925
01:27:53,280 --> 01:27:55,399
As you command my Bey.

926
01:27:58,080 --> 01:28:00,359
Give the letter and come back, Cerkutay.

927
01:28:01,160 --> 01:28:02,119
Come on.

928
01:28:13,400 --> 01:28:16,279
If you say something wrong...

929
01:28:17,080 --> 01:28:21,399
...I will cut your throat before
you finish your sentence.

930
01:28:25,080 --> 01:28:26,879
Come on.

931
01:28:32,920 --> 01:28:35,279
Once the army is scattered...

932
01:28:35,280 --> 01:28:39,599
...you're going to go to the secret
headquarters to get prepared.

933
01:28:40,720 --> 01:28:45,399
We'll see how much the commanders
love their relatives.

934
01:28:45,920 --> 01:28:50,239
We will make them go through every move
they intended to use on us.

935
01:28:50,240 --> 01:28:53,079
What about Turgut Bey?

936
01:28:53,080 --> 01:28:56,079
We'll take him too, don't worry.

937
01:28:57,120 --> 01:28:59,439
Once the army is scattered...

938
01:28:59,440 --> 01:29:01,799
We still have time for now.

939
01:29:08,600 --> 01:29:12,679
Carvers will start to throw the coins
with the first sun rays in the morning.

940
01:29:12,680 --> 01:29:14,799
We should have everything ready.

941
01:29:14,800 --> 01:29:18,559
We don't have anything missing,
don't worry.

942
01:29:19,160 --> 01:29:20,719
Go tell the Alps that...

943
01:29:20,840 --> 01:29:24,599
...they will move the silvers here
from the mines at dawn.

944
01:29:25,200 --> 01:29:26,799
As you command, mother.

945
01:29:27,000 --> 01:29:28,999
As you command.

946
01:29:29,360 --> 01:29:31,159
Our mission is important.

947
01:29:31,280 --> 01:29:33,839
Everyone in Yenisehir is waiting for it.

948
01:29:33,840 --> 01:29:37,999
For that reason, be careful.

949
01:29:39,600 --> 01:29:43,759
We have a lot of friends but we
have more enemies.

950
01:29:45,120 --> 01:29:47,759
May Allah help us.

951
01:29:49,520 --> 01:29:51,239
Amen.

952
01:29:58,200 --> 01:30:00,119
Tell me..

953
01:30:02,800 --> 01:30:04,239
...Bengi Hatun.

954
01:30:05,400 --> 01:30:08,279
What happened here in our absence?

955
01:30:10,880 --> 01:30:14,599
You must have heard about
what happened, Mother Sultan.

956
01:30:15,800 --> 01:30:18,599
You have eyes and ears everywhere.

957
01:30:19,760 --> 01:30:22,799
But the information
I am going to give you is different.

958
01:30:28,040 --> 01:30:29,439
What is it?

959
01:30:30,040 --> 01:30:31,559
Osman.

960
01:30:34,240 --> 01:30:36,199
He won't stop.

961
01:30:37,960 --> 01:30:40,559
What he is doing now...

962
01:30:42,800 --> 01:30:44,679
He is printing coins.

963
01:30:50,400 --> 01:30:52,999
What do you mean he prints coins?

964
01:30:53,400 --> 01:30:54,759
He can't dare to do that!

965
01:30:54,760 --> 01:30:56,319
He did, Mother Sultan.

966
01:30:56,720 --> 01:30:58,519
Malhun is taking care of that.

967
01:30:58,760 --> 01:31:00,519
They are working hard.

968
01:31:00,520 --> 01:31:02,359
They took care of everything.

969
01:31:02,360 --> 01:31:03,999
Bad manners!

970
01:31:04,440 --> 01:31:06,999
Do you know what this means, Bengi Hatun?

971
01:31:07,320 --> 01:31:10,679
It means that he is not acknowledging
the Seljuk .state anymore!

972
01:31:13,600 --> 01:31:16,839
This means that he is on his on now!

973
01:31:17,760 --> 01:31:22,199
Osman manages to turn all kinds
of defeats beneficial for himself.

974
01:31:22,600 --> 01:31:27,399
Now he is trying to win the favor of
immigrants of Yenisehir with a soup kitchen.

975
01:31:28,720 --> 01:31:32,399
Yenisehir took many
migrations, Mother Sultan.

976
01:31:32,600 --> 01:31:34,199
Osman is getting more powerful.

977
01:31:36,080 --> 01:31:37,519
Osman!

978
01:31:38,600 --> 01:31:43,359
He is still not aware of whom he is facing

979
01:31:48,640 --> 01:31:50,599
We need to stop Osman.

980
01:31:50,800 --> 01:31:52,759
Or it will be late.

981
01:32:01,600 --> 01:32:03,319
He will -stop.

982
01:32:04,840 --> 01:32:07,039
Osman will stop.

983
01:32:10,160 --> 01:32:14,999
First, we will stop the printing
of the coins!

984
01:32:15,800 --> 01:32:17,839
We will stop that.

985
01:32:20,360 --> 01:32:24,439
Now listen to me refully, Bengi Hatu

986
01:33:07,480 --> 01:33:13,399
Come on, we need to hurry. Malhun Hatun
asked us to return with daylight.

987
01:33:15,840 --> 01:33:17,839
You did well, Aybars.

988
01:33:18,080 --> 01:33:19,479
You were right.

989
01:33:20,320 --> 01:33:22,399
This is where Malhun's iron is.

990
01:33:23,400 --> 01:33:25,599
How are we going to move away the alps?

991
01:33:26,200 --> 01:33:27,399
Should we kill them?

992
01:33:27,600 --> 01:33:30,599
I thought something forthat. Don't worry.

993
01:33:33,000 --> 01:33:35,079
Alps, come on.

994
01:33:44,600 --> 01:33:46,919
We will stop them, come on.

995
01:33:46,920 --> 01:33:47,919
Come with me.

996
01:34:03,960 --> 01:34:05,839
Peace be with you, brothers.

997
01:34:05,840 --> 01:34:07,119
Peace be upon you.

998
01:34:07,120 --> 01:34:08,159
Who are you?

999
01:34:08,320 --> 01:34:09,379
Malhun Hatun sent me.

1000
01:34:09,399 --> 01:34:13,329
She said 1 carriage wouldn't be enough,
so told us to bring the second carriage.

1001
01:34:14,160 --> 01:34:17,159
Okay, we will leave, so you can bring it.

1002
01:34:17,640 --> 01:34:21,079
She told us to bring her
the loaded carriage.

1003
01:34:24,920 --> 01:34:29,399
Then take the carriage,
we will follow you after filling this one.

1004
01:34:30,360 --> 01:34:32,159
Come on, safe travels.

1005
01:34:32,480 --> 01:34:33,879
Come on brothers.

1006
01:34:42,040 --> 01:34:43,599
Come on.

1007
01:35:15,200 --> 01:35:17,679
This will be so embarrassing
for you Osman.

1008
01:35:18,600 --> 01:35:20,799
This time no one can save you.

1009
01:35:21,840 --> 01:35:22,759
Come on Alps.

1010
01:35:24,160 --> 01:35:25,399
Change the baskets.

1011
01:35:31,640 --> 01:35:33,959
Won't they know these are damaged?

1012
01:35:35,440 --> 01:35:36,799
They won't.

1013
01:35:39,000 --> 01:35:41,039
Mother Sultan says..

1014
01:35:42,200 --> 01:35:42,999
...these...

1015
01:35:43,720 --> 01:35:45,519
...are worthy when they're melted.

1016
01:35:57,720 --> 01:35:59,119
They’re both the same.

1017
01:36:00,520 --> 01:36:02,719
But when this melts, it's trash.

1018
01:36:03,600 --> 01:36:05,359
But when this melts it's valuable.

1019
01:36:11,260 --> 01:36:12,219
Come on.

1020
01:36:12,600 --> 01:36:14,359
Hurry up! Come on!

1021
01:36:31,800 --> 01:36:33,999
Finish preparations Celali.

1022
01:36:34,000 --> 01:36:35,279
We'll leave.

1023
01:36:51,560 --> 01:36:53,799
Hadrath Mother Sultan...

1024
01:36:54,840 --> 01:36:56,559
Forgive me but...

1025
01:36:57,480 --> 01:37:01,039
...I don't feel good about this.

1026
01:37:03,200 --> 01:37:07,279
What if Nayman's playing a game?

1027
01:37:11,920 --> 01:37:14,559
You've been sayin the same thing.

1028
01:37:17,560 --> 01:37:19,999
How do you know this is a game of Nayman?

1029
01:37:55,720 --> 01:37:58,319
What's your point?

1030
01:38:00,280 --> 01:38:03,039
The rising sun of Great Seljuk.

1031
01:38:03,560 --> 01:38:05,839
This poor servant..

1032
01:38:05,840 --> 01:38:08,759
...only aims to save your life.

1033
01:38:08,760 --> 01:38:10,759
That's all.

1034
01:38:11,920 --> 01:38:13,279
However...

1035
01:38:14,040 --> 01:38:15,999
...I was with that infidel...

1036
01:38:16,920 --> 01:38:19,999
...long enough to get to know him.

1037
01:38:23,040 --> 01:38:25,079
If he wanted to trick us..

1038
01:38:25,680 --> 01:38:28,519
...he would have done it by now.

1039
01:38:28,840 --> 01:38:30,119
Bayindir.

1040
01:38:32,520 --> 01:38:35,039
But you should feel at ease.

1041
01:38:35,960 --> 01:38:37,999
I won't die today.

1042
01:38:41,200 --> 01:38:45,399
Today I will become the ruler of this land.

1043
01:38:46,600 --> 01:38:49,039
That's why we're going to the council.

1044
01:38:51,320 --> 01:38:52,559
But..

1045
01:38:53,840 --> 01:38:56,599
...if you have fear in your heart...

1046
01:38:57,520 --> 01:38:58,599
...stay.

1047
01:39:00,200 --> 01:39:02,599
Our path is a hard one.

1048
01:39:09,240 --> 01:39:12,959
Those who have fear in their hearts...

1049
01:39:14,560 --> 01:39:16,879
...can't walk Bayindir.

1050
01:39:19,680 --> 01:39:22,279
Your path is my own Mother Sultan.

1051
01:39:22,800 --> 01:39:24,639
That's all I know.

1052
01:39:42,600 --> 01:39:43,959
What's going on Osman?

1053
01:39:47,040 --> 01:39:47,679
Bala.

1054
01:39:48,000 --> 01:39:51,319
It's time to keep the promise I made you.

1055
01:39:51,840 --> 01:39:53,279
What promise?

1056
01:39:54,800 --> 01:39:57,799
I made a promise to you when
we were in that cruel's inn.

1057
01:39:58,560 --> 01:40:01,159
I'm going to keep it now.

1058
01:40:03,200 --> 01:40:04,319
What promise?

1059
01:40:05,000 --> 01:40:06,199
Don't you remember?

1060
01:40:06,800 --> 01:40:08,439
No I don't.

1061
01:40:08,440 --> 01:40:10,239
Remind me.

1062
01:40:10,960 --> 01:40:12,479
Okay then.

1063
01:40:12,920 --> 01:40:15,599
You'll remember when you see it.

1064
01:40:16,080 --> 01:40:16,879
Besides...

1065
01:40:17,800 --> 01:40:19,799
...let's see if your wounds are healed.

1066
01:40:19,800 --> 01:40:20,999
I'm okay.

1067
01:40:21,000 --> 01:40:23,479
I would beat you even in this state Osman Bey.

1068
01:40:23,480 --> 01:40:25,799
If you say so.

1069
01:40:26,120 --> 01:40:27,919
Yeltutan?

1070
01:40:27,920 --> 01:40:28,799
Come on son.

1071
01:40:29,280 --> 01:40:31,039
Are you ready?

1072
01:40:31,040 --> 01:40:34,079
Alacan did you hear what he said?

1073
01:40:34,080 --> 01:40:35,999
Come on dear.

1074
01:40:36,800 --> 01:40:38,879
Come on.

1075
01:41:49,920 --> 01:41:52,639
We're going to throw those to them who else?

1076
01:42:07,000 --> 01:42:08,399
Konur.

1077
01:42:08,799 --> 01:42:09,799
Brother.

1078
01:42:10,200 --> 01:42:13,439
You didn’t tell us about the inkwell issue.

1079
01:42:14,720 --> 01:42:16,999
Allah Allah.

1080
01:42:17,320 --> 01:42:19,439
He's right Konur.

1081
01:42:20,120 --> 01:42:21,959
You just change the subject.

1082
01:42:23,080 --> 01:42:24,639
Brothers.

1083
01:42:24,840 --> 01:42:26,599
He's keeping it a secret.

1084
01:42:26,600 --> 01:42:29,639
He always has some secrets.

1085
01:42:33,080 --> 01:42:36,049
Konur doesn't like to
talk about his accomplishments.

1086
01:42:36,049 --> 01:42:38,659
But you have no other option
but to tell us, Konur.

1087
01:42:42,720 --> 01:42:45,039
While you were fighting
at the headquarters...

1088
01:42:45,040 --> 01:42:47,039
...I was fighting for the ink pen.

1089
01:42:47,280 --> 01:42:49,279
I don't know what you're asking.

1090
01:42:49,280 --> 01:42:52,519
It's clear you went through a tough fight.

1091
01:42:53,000 --> 01:42:57,359
If it was Cerkutay he would've talked
about it nonstop for 15 days.

1092
01:43:07,800 --> 01:43:10,399
I win every fight I get into...

1093
01:43:10,400 --> 01:43:13,199
...and tell about it but...

1094
01:43:15,170 --> 01:43:18,599
..I'm in an undecided fight right now.

1095
01:43:19,800 --> 01:43:22,799
You'll see it all when I win anyways.

1096
01:43:40,360 --> 01:43:43,479
We called him lunatic for too long.

1097
01:43:43,880 --> 01:43:46,239
Do you think we might've
turned him into one?

1098
01:43:50,000 --> 01:43:52,999
After what great Nayman does to you...

1099
01:43:53,400 --> 01:43:55,679
...the ones who die will be lucky.

1100
01:43:55,680 --> 01:43:58,199
Those who are left alive
will all be lunatic.

1101
01:43:58,200 --> 01:43:59,319
Shut it.

1102
01:44:02,240 --> 01:44:05,879
Do you think you can take us to great
Nayman's headquarters...

1103
01:44:06,040 --> 01:44:09,599
...and get out of there alive?

1104
01:44:09,600 --> 01:44:11,199
All of you.

1105
01:44:11,200 --> 01:44:14,039
All of you will die.

1106
01:44:16,320 --> 01:44:20,919
Did you think that my Bey
was going to take you there?

1107
01:44:23,600 --> 01:44:26,479
You're the ones who will die.

1108
01:44:30,440 --> 01:44:32,119
My bey's order.

1109
01:44:32,560 --> 01:44:34,319
Take everything...

1110
01:44:34,360 --> 01:44:37,399
...with a mark on them.

1111
01:44:38,000 --> 01:44:39,799
Nayman and his beys...

1112
01:44:39,800 --> 01:44:43,319
...will see that we have the commanders
of their blood in our hands.

1113
01:44:57,400 --> 01:45:02,039
Stay put or I'll let Cerkutay deal
with you.

1114
01:45:42,120 --> 01:45:44,719
What are you looking at, Nayman's dog?

1115
01:45:46,760 --> 01:45:49,319
I'm talking to you!

1116
01:45:51,920 --> 01:45:55,119
Can’t you hear?

1117
01:45:55,640 --> 01:45:59,679
Are you only brave when you're crowded?

1118
01:46:02,800 --> 01:46:07,279
Aren't you even brave enough to answer
me on your own?

1119
01:46:07,960 --> 01:46:09,679
Nayman's little puppy.

1120
01:46:11,960 --> 01:46:13,519
Soldiers!

1121
01:46:18,520 --> 01:46:22,039
I will take all of you down for what
you've done to my Alps!

1122
01:46:23,200 --> 01:46:25,439
I will destroy you!

1123
01:46:25,640 --> 01:46:28,679
I will kill all of you...

1124
01:46:29,400 --> 01:46:31,639
...one by one!

1125
01:46:47,400 --> 01:46:48,319
Filthy Turk!

1126
01:46:50,560 --> 01:46:52,079
Let me go!

1127
01:46:52,600 --> 01:46:54,039
Let me go

1128
01:47:20,640 --> 01:47:23,479
He cut the ropes with this bone.

1129
01:47:28,640 --> 01:47:30,679
Where's my army?

1130
01:47:31,800 --> 01:47:33,279
Why aren't they here?

1131
01:47:33,520 --> 01:47:36,239
They should have been here .by now, but-

1132
01:47:37,360 --> 01:47:39,959
You're going to find out where my army is!

1133
01:47:54,160 --> 01:47:57,399
Don't you trust us at all, Nayman?

1134
01:47:58,560 --> 01:48:00,039
Don't worry, Nayman.

1135
01:48:00,200 --> 01:48:02,439
Nothing can stop that army.

1136
01:48:02,800 --> 01:48:04,839
They will be here soon.

1137
01:48:05,320 --> 01:48:09,359
No one can dare stand in.their way.

1138
01:48:12,120 --> 01:48:14,079
No one can..

1139
01:48:14,280 --> 01:48:18,599
...stop the army with swords...

1140
01:48:20,600 --> 01:48:22,759
However...

1141
01:48:23,080 --> 01:48:25,999
...they might be tricked.

1142
01:48:27,480 --> 01:48:30,039
Who could do such a thing.

1143
01:48:35,400 --> 01:48:39,479
Osman.

1144
01:49:12,680 --> 01:49:15,239
I have no problem defeating enemies...

1145
01:49:15,440 --> 01:49:18,559
...but I still can't figure out a way to
defeat my Hatun.

1146
01:49:19,000 --> 01:49:21,199
MashAllah.

1147
01:49:21,520 --> 01:49:23,319
Once again, I'm no match for you.

1148
01:49:23,560 --> 01:49:26,199
Indeed.

1149
01:49:30,880 --> 01:49:31,959
Alright...

1150
01:49:32,160 --> 01:49:34,399
Alright now...

1151
01:49:43,920 --> 01:49:46,999
Come here.

1152
01:49:49,960 --> 01:49:52,359
How nice is that?

1153
01:49:52,600 --> 01:49:56,159
MashAllah...

1154
01:50:06,520 --> 01:50:11,199
I couldn't even think of coming here
with everything that's going on.

1155
01:50:21,960 --> 01:50:24,519
Look at them.

1156
01:50:34,200 --> 01:50:36,319
Look how beautiful they are.

1157
01:50:37,440 --> 01:50:40,439
Bala, I promised you.

1158
01:50:41,000 --> 01:50:43,799
That I would bring you
to see these flowers.

1159
01:50:44,400 --> 01:50:46,199
Here you go.

1160
01:50:59,200 --> 01:51:01,799
We should keep our promises quickly.

1161
01:51:01,800 --> 01:51:04,119
We shouldn't wait on them.

1162
01:51:04,640 --> 01:51:08,119
Death is close to us like our breath.

1163
01:51:09,000 --> 01:51:12,119
That's right.

1164
01:51:12,680 --> 01:51:18,799
People think it's not close,
but you realize it when you almost die.

1165
01:51:20,080 --> 01:51:22,119
Being close to death does not scare us.

1166
01:51:22,760 --> 01:51:26,239
You just think about the ones
you leave behind.

1167
01:51:26,560 --> 01:51:29,599
Death is for all of us.

1168
01:51:29,760 --> 01:51:32,759
But separation, longing.

1169
01:51:33,320 --> 01:51:34,999
That's the hard part.

1170
01:51:37,520 --> 01:51:41,039
May Allah not test us with that,
InshAllah.

1171
01:51:41,040 --> 01:51:44,279
Amen, may Allah give you
a long life, my Bey.

1172
01:51:44,680 --> 01:51:46,399
Ameen.

1173
01:51:47,840 --> 01:51:51,879
But when I saw you among flames like that.

1174
01:51:52,440 --> 01:51:56,439
Bala, you, the children...

1175
01:52:01,200 --> 01:52:04,359
Being a father is harder than battles.

1176
01:52:05,160 --> 01:52:07,719
You were the winner of that
tough battle, Osman Bey.

1177
01:52:08,400 --> 01:52:13,719
Your children are brave
and strong like you.

1178
01:52:50,800 --> 01:52:51,799
My Bey.

1179
01:52:55,840 --> 01:52:58,839
We got word from our scouting alps.
They are on the move.

1180
01:52:59,400 --> 01:53:01,599
So it's time for the duty, huh?

1181
01:53:03,200 --> 01:53:04,999
Time for duty.

1182
01:53:07,280 --> 01:53:09,119
Did you prepare the equipment?

1183
01:53:09,800 --> 01:53:11,399
Here, Osman Bey.

1184
01:53:11,800 --> 01:53:13,519
Who is on the move?

1185
01:53:13,760 --> 01:53:15,759
What duty is this, Osman Bey?

1186
01:53:15,960 --> 01:53:16,999
Ismihan.

1187
01:53:17,800 --> 01:53:21,399
She stopped the army
I asked from Sultan Alaeddin.

1188
01:53:21,880 --> 01:53:23,879
Nayman invites her to the council.

1189
01:53:24,720 --> 01:53:26,759
If he takes the seal..

1190
01:53:27,600 --> 01:53:30,199
...then he would give her
the power she wanted.

1191
01:53:30,600 --> 01:53:33,279
And he would involve
Ismihan into the council.

1192
01:53:37,880 --> 01:53:39,639
What's in the bag?

1193
01:53:51,920 --> 01:53:55,599
Disguises that would make Ismihan
believe Nayman attacked him.

1194
01:53:59,880 --> 01:54:02,079
EyvAllah Osman Bey.

1195
01:54:02,600 --> 01:54:05,839
So we just did not come here
to pick flowers, huh?

1196
01:54:14,600 --> 01:54:15,839
No.

1197
01:54:16,520 --> 01:54:20,639
What are you waiting for?
Go and pick some flowers for Alcicek

1198
01:54:22,600 --> 01:54:23,879
As you command my Bey.

1199
01:54:37,120 --> 01:54:38,199
My Bala.

1200
01:54:39,080 --> 01:54:41,399
It's your duty now.

1201
01:54:42,560 --> 01:54:45,399
You will stop Ismihan
from entering the council.

1202
01:54:45,800 --> 01:54:47,599
Don't worry.

1203
01:54:51,160 --> 01:54:52,839
Pick them up faster.

1204
01:55:02,600 --> 01:55:05,879
Osman's time is up today.

1205
01:55:06,640 --> 01:55:11,039
He always has a plan.

1206
01:55:14,760 --> 01:55:18,199
The commanders of our
blood leads the army.

1207
01:55:20,800 --> 01:55:23,399
No one can stop our progress.

1208
01:55:25,400 --> 01:55:26,519
Great Nayman.

1209
01:55:27,160 --> 01:55:28,839
The army will come.

1210
01:55:29,240 --> 01:55:30,839
But tell us.

1211
01:55:31,000 --> 01:55:32,799
Who will replace Talay?

1212
01:55:34,600 --> 01:55:37,959
Whoever gives the seal to me.

1213
01:55:43,320 --> 01:55:45,599
Will you let a Turk step in?

1214
01:55:46,560 --> 01:55:49,759
Empires don't care about race.

1215
01:55:50,400 --> 01:55:52,519
Great Empires..

1216
01:55:52,720 --> 01:55:54,519
...are ruled with competence.

1217
01:55:58,320 --> 01:56:02,239
Ismihan deserves this position.

1218
01:56:06,360 --> 01:56:07,999
I'll give her that power.

1219
01:56:09,600 --> 01:56:13,679
She will rule the borders in my name.

1220
01:56:15,880 --> 01:56:19,039
Send Warriors to welcome Ismihan.

1221
01:56:21,400 --> 01:56:23,559
There will be no mistakes.

1222
01:56:26,200 --> 01:56:27,999
A Turk in the council?

1223
01:56:30,240 --> 01:56:31,439
That has never happened!

1224
01:56:32,840 --> 01:56:36,999
We'll do many more things
that never happened.

1225
01:56:37,600 --> 01:56:39,599
Many things.

1226
01:56:40,200 --> 01:56:41,599
You will obey.

1227
01:56:42,400 --> 01:56:44,599
And we'll praise Genghis.

1228
01:56:47,320 --> 01:56:50,999
But don't you worry.

1229
01:56:51,600 --> 01:56:53,639
He'll kill Turgut for us..

1230
01:56:54,400 --> 01:56:56,599
...and prove her loyalty.

1231
01:57:01,200 --> 01:57:02,159
Kan!

1232
01:57:04,080 --> 01:57:06,279
Let Turgut in.

1233
01:57:41,000 --> 01:57:41,999
Now.

1234
01:57:50,000 --> 01:57:51,479
Soldiers!

1235
01:57:52,200 --> 01:57:53,479
Attack!

1236
01:58:00,480 --> 01:58:01,199
Warriors.

1237
01:58:02,000 --> 01:58:05,319
We shouldn't have trusted Nayman,
Hadrat Mother Sultan.

1238
01:58:18,040 --> 01:58:21,119
There's too many. We must retreat.

1239
01:58:28,160 --> 01:58:30,519
I'll take my revenge.

1240
01:58:32,720 --> 01:58:34,919
Come on. Retreat!

1241
01:58:36,280 --> 01:58:37,759
Come on.

1242
01:58:42,000 --> 01:58:43,439
Protect Mother Sultan.

1243
01:59:14,400 --> 01:59:15,759
Run Ismihan run!

1244
01:59:18,760 --> 01:59:21,559
The only reason that arrow is
not in your heart...

1245
01:59:21,960 --> 01:59:23,799
...is Sultan Alaeddin's shadow.

1246
01:59:25,600 --> 01:59:29,519
When the time comes,
you won't run from our justice.

1247
01:59:42,120 --> 01:59:45,079
Thank Allah we're saved.

1248
01:59:45,720 --> 01:59:47,039
Mother Sultan'Hadrath.

1249
01:59:47,560 --> 01:59:50,359
We barely escaped. Barely

1250
01:59:51,040 --> 01:59:54,239
I told you. We shouldn't
have trusted Nayman.

1251
01:59:54,800 --> 01:59:56,919
Shat up Bayindir. Shut up

1252
01:59:56,920 --> 01:59:58,799
How could Nayman do this?

1253
02:00:00,680 --> 02:00:04,559
Mother Sultan Hadrath.
He wants to be the only ruler.

1254
02:00:04,560 --> 02:00:06,559
Nayman doesn't want to share power.

1255
02:00:32,440 --> 02:00:34,919
You wore alp clothes before.

1256
02:00:35,600 --> 02:00:38,119
And now warrior clothes.

1257
02:00:38,840 --> 02:00:42,179
I was wondering which clothes
I was going to be seeing you tomorrow.

1258
02:00:42,360 --> 02:00:45,879
You should look at yourself first.

1259
02:00:47,400 --> 02:00:50,999
I was thinking whatever
you wore suited you, but...

1260
02:00:51,320 --> 02:00:55,039
...turns out you are the one who make
the clothes look good, Alcicek Hatun.

1261
02:01:14,120 --> 02:01:14,839
My bey.

1262
02:01:14,840 --> 02:01:16,799
Alps will stand around the headquarters.

1263
02:01:16,800 --> 02:01:19,009
They will attack at the
smallest of the moves.

1264
02:01:19,009 --> 02:01:21,829
And the rest will tend to them.

1265
02:01:22,280 --> 02:01:23,919
As you wish my bey.

1266
02:01:23,920 --> 02:01:25,119
Konur.

1267
02:01:25,120 --> 02:01:26,399
Cerkutay.

1268
02:01:26,800 --> 02:01:28,399
Baysungur.

1269
02:01:28,400 --> 02:01:30,759
You'll keep your hands on your weapon.

1270
02:01:31,240 --> 02:01:33,759
If they aim a sword at Turgut Bey...

1271
02:01:33,760 --> 02:01:35,999
...you’ll end them.

1272
02:01:36,840 --> 02:01:38,439
We'll take Turgut Bey.

1273
02:01:38,440 --> 02:01:40,279
This will end today.

1274
02:01:40,280 --> 02:01:43,010
The end will come to those who...

1275
02:01:43,010 --> 02:01:44,869
...wish to spill blood
on these lands.

1276
02:01:44,869 --> 02:01:45,919
Come on.

1277
02:01:55,200 --> 02:01:57,359
Keep your eyes peeled.

1278
02:01:58,040 --> 02:02:01,199
No one should know we did this.

1279
02:02:02,000 --> 02:02:03,599
Aunt.

1280
02:02:03,600 --> 02:02:05,599
Why are we doing this?

1281
02:02:05,680 --> 02:02:08,439
No one would benefit from those coins.

1282
02:02:08,440 --> 02:02:09,879
Don't ask like you don't know.

1283
02:02:09,880 --> 02:02:11,599
Do whatever I

1284
02:02:11,600 --> 02:02:13,999
Don't question the rest niece.

1285
02:02:14,800 --> 02:02:17,079
To gain power...

1286
02:02:17,560 --> 02:02:19,759
...we need Mother Sultan.

1287
02:02:20,960 --> 02:02:23,999
We'll do whatever she says.

1288
02:02:24,800 --> 02:02:27,199
There's no other way.

1289
02:02:30,880 --> 02:02:32,559
Bengi Hatun.

1290
02:02:32,760 --> 02:02:34,399
Welcome.

1291
02:02:35,120 --> 02:02:37,359
Welcome to you too.

1292
02:02:38,240 --> 02:02:41,919
I came to bring the bags
Ayse Hatun send to Alcicek Hatun.

1293
02:02:42,360 --> 02:02:43,599
Good.

1294
02:02:44,000 --> 02:02:45,719
This is your tribe too.

1295
02:02:46,000 --> 02:02:48,719
I didn't ask you why you came right?

1296
02:02:49,800 --> 02:02:51,599
eave then.

1297
02:02:52,360 --> 02:02:53,599
I shouldn't be late.

1298
02:02:54,280 --> 02:02:55,599
Go on.

1299
02:03:03,960 --> 02:03:05,879
Why are they doing this?

1300
02:03:17,480 --> 02:03:19,999
This was Osman's last day to...

1301
02:03:20,000 --> 02:03:20,999
...leave...

1302
02:03:21,000 --> 02:03:24,599
...his weapons and swore his loyalty.

1303
02:03:25,280 --> 02:03:26,599
He didn't come.

1304
02:03:27,400 --> 02:03:32,419
And he will start to
pay for it with Turgut’s death.

1305
02:03:35,760 --> 02:03:38,279
Do you-see someone...

1306
02:03:39,400 --> 02:03:42,199
...who is not willing to do so?

1307
02:03:46,000 --> 02:03:48,079
I don't.

1308
02:03:56,360 --> 02:03:59,039
My armies are on the way.

1309
02:03:59,680 --> 02:04:06,039
I'm going to flood Osman's
lands with blood.

1310
02:04:08,400 --> 02:04:13,199
Those you don't obey
are destined to die Turgut.

1311
02:04:13,360 --> 02:04:14,879
Don't worry.

1312
02:04:14,960 --> 02:04:17,639
You're going to pay that price.

1313
02:04:18,800 --> 02:04:20,439
You always...

1314
02:04:21,120 --> 02:04:24,719
...talk about spilling
innocent people's blood.

1315
02:04:28,080 --> 02:04:31,999
Did you ever think about
how you'll pay for that?

1316
02:04:34,800 --> 02:04:36,479
You'll...

1317
02:04:38,920 --> 02:04:41,519
...pay for it...

1318
02:04:45,160 --> 02:04:47,359
...dying...

1319
02:04:48,960 --> 02:04:51,239
...painfully by our hands.

1320
02:04:52,520 --> 02:04:53,919
But...

1321
02:04:53,920 --> 02:04:57,999
...you will be killed by Ismihan.

1322
02:05:00,480 --> 02:05:05,199
I'm always going to
make you kill each other.

1323
02:05:05,760 --> 02:05:08,799
Who can take me to account?

1324
02:05:09,960 --> 02:05:11,599
Who knows?

1325
02:05:13,880 --> 02:05:16,119
Maybe I will.

1326
02:05:49,600 --> 02:05:52,439
Osman Bey is here!

1327
02:06:04,320 --> 02:06:08,119
Brother...

1328
02:06:10,520 --> 02:06:12,919
Osman is here.

1329
02:06:18,160 --> 02:06:21,319
Osman Bey...

1330
02:06:23,960 --> 02:06:26,479
Let's see...

1331
02:06:43,280 --> 02:06:46,079
Oh Allah, let us succeed...

1332
02:06:54,200 --> 02:06:56,359
In the name of Allah..

1333
02:07:01,750 --> 02:07:04,519
NAYMAN’S BASE

1334
02:07:49,040 --> 02:07:51,519
Osman!

1335
02:07:51,800 --> 02:07:54,919
Didn't you expect to see me?

1336
02:07:55,400 --> 02:07:58,319
Your sword is still in it's sheath.

1337
02:07:58,840 --> 02:08:00,439
I see that...

1338
02:08:01,040 --> 02:08:03,100
...you're hot here to surrender.

1339
02:08:20,840 --> 02:08:24,119
You've taken Turgut as a prisoner...

1340
02:08:24,280 --> 02:08:27,279
..and went against my home!

1341
02:08:32,880 --> 02:08:34,999
Boran.

1342
02:08:43,360 --> 02:08:46,679
Put those away!

1343
02:08:46,800 --> 02:08:49,559
Soldiers.

1344
02:08:50,940 --> 02:08:51,879
Here...

1345
02:08:54,600 --> 02:08:58,099
These are from the commanders
of the army that you're waiting for.

1346
02:09:08,040 --> 02:09:10,959
These, too.

1347
02:09:14,960 --> 02:09:18,599
I've captured your commanders...

1348
02:09:26,120 --> 02:09:28,919
...and the army you're waiting
for will not come.

1349
02:09:41,440 --> 02:09:42,959
My nephew

1350
02:09:50,600 --> 02:09:53,399
This belongs to my brother!

1351
02:09:57,480 --> 02:09:58,599
Stop him, Nayman!

1352
02:09:58,600 --> 02:10:02,119
Save our sons and nephews

1353
02:10:02,240 --> 02:10:04,079
Nayman-

1354
02:10:04,480 --> 02:10:08,279
Our families, Nayman....
Our brothers!

1355
02:10:25,040 --> 02:10:29,159
The soldiers you called to spill
blood on my home...

1356
02:10:30,000 --> 02:10:32,719
..have all gone back to their homes.

1357
02:10:34,360 --> 02:10:37,119
I sent them all away.

1358
02:10:38,840 --> 02:10:41,199
The life of your commanders
depend on my words.

1359
02:10:41,440 --> 02:10:44,159
Save them, Nayman.

1360
02:10:44,160 --> 02:10:45,679
Do something.

1361
02:10:47,000 --> 02:10:49,559
What do you want, Osman?

1362
02:10:50,280 --> 02:10:52,679
You will release Turgut...

1363
02:10:56,520 --> 02:10:58,799
...and the Beys will get their
commanders back.

1364
02:10:59,400 --> 02:11:01,359
Otherwise..

1365
02:11:02,000 --> 02:11:05,039
...even the seal won’t help you.

1366
02:11:07,440 --> 02:11:08,719
Nayman...

1367
02:11:08,840 --> 02:11:09,839
Mighty Naymaö

1368
02:11:10,080 --> 02:11:12,079
Stop him.

1369
02:11:17,520 --> 02:11:20,279
You're in deep waters.

1370
02:11:21,160 --> 02:11:25,959
You're just making the war bigger...

1371
02:11:26,800 --> 02:11:29,879
...instead of surrendering.

1372
02:11:30,280 --> 02:11:32,399
The price you'll pay will be great!

1373
02:11:32,520 --> 02:11:34,719
No...

1374
02:11:35,440 --> 02:11:37,999
The war was already big enough.

1375
02:11:38,720 --> 02:11:43,719
is a battle betwee right and wrong.

1376
02:11:45,200 --> 02:11:47,199
But I swear that..

1377
02:11:47,840 --> 02:11:50,199
...no matter how great...

1378
02:11:50,440 --> 02:11:53,359
...or how strong you are...

1379
02:11:54,320 --> 02:11:57,479
...the winner of this war...

1380
02:11:58,040 --> 02:12:01,039
...can only be us.

1381
02:12:03,920 --> 02:12:07,999
Now release Turgut!

1382
02:12:10,920 --> 02:12:13,239
Or the commanders will die.

1383
02:12:14,280 --> 02:12:16,599
The choice is yours.

1384
02:12:18,880 --> 02:12:21,479
They're our blood, Nayman.

1385
02:12:22,400 --> 02:12:25,319
Let Turgut go.

1386
02:12:45,400 --> 02:12:48,079
Soldiers!

1387
02:13:13,800 --> 02:13:15,799
I knew that you'd come, brother.

1388
02:13:16,200 --> 02:13:19,399
Thank you.

1389
02:13:24,560 --> 02:13:27,639
You might have won today...

1390
02:13:28,440 --> 02:13:32,319
..but I will be the one
who wins in the long run.

1391
02:13:34,280 --> 02:13:39,639
When we reach for our swords,
we always become the winner!

1392
02:13:44,692 --> 02:13:59,072
Visit our website for more: turkision.com